♪ About the tremor ♪

26
00:03:12,500 --> 00:03:13,875
♪ Music ends ♪

27
00:03:17,708 --> 00:03:19,167
[church bells ringing]

28
00:03:26,792 --> 00:03:28,458
♪ Music begins ♪

29
00:03:34,667 --> 00:03:36,292
[teacher speaking French]
Révérence.

30
00:03:38,375 --> 00:03:39,583
♪ Music continues ♪

31
00:03:42,083 --> 00:03:44,125
[teacher] Very good. That's all for today, girls.

32
00:03:46,833 --> 00:03:48,667
[teacher] Don't forget your bracelets.

33
00:03:50,125 --> 00:03:51,417
♪ Music continues ♪

34
00:04:05,208 --> 00:04:06,542
♪ Music continues ♪

35
00:04:17,208 --> 00:04:18,500
♪ Music ends ♪

36
00:04:21,083 --> 00:04:22,833
- [dancer] Goodbye.
- [student] Bye.

37
00:04:24,250 --> 00:04:25,708
[whistle blowing]

38
00:04:38,292 --> 00:04:39,625
[brakes screeching]

39
00:04:48,208 --> 00:04:49,208
[vendor] Hello.

40
00:04:49,292 --> 00:04:51,000
- [teacher] Is my order ready?
- [shopkeeper] Of course, Martina.

41
00:04:51,083 --> 00:04:52,958
[shopkeeper] Marta, please ring them up.

42
00:04:54,500 --> 00:04:56,167
[man] Could I have some cigarettes, please?

43
00:04:59,250 --> 00:05:00,417
Everything's fine.

44
00:05:01,667 --> 00:05:03,167
[Marta] Are the white ones okay?

45
00:05:05,333 --> 00:05:06,875
[Marta] Fifty-five pesos, please.

46
00:05:06,958 --> 00:05:08,833
[shopkeeper] That'll be 342 pesos.

47
00:05:10,333 --> 00:05:12,125
- [shopkeeper] Thank you.
- [man] Thank you.

48
00:05:14,542 --> 00:05:15,875
[shopkeeper] Your change.

49
00:05:19,708 --> 00:05:21,583
- [vendor] Martina, your things.
- [Martina] Oh...

50
00:05:21,917 --> 00:05:23,917
Yes, just a moment.

51
00:05:25,375 --> 00:05:27,167
- [Martina] Thank you.
- [vendor] See you later.

52
00:05:30,958 --> 00:05:31,958
[birds chirping]

53
00:05:36,750 --> 00:05:37,750
It's hot.

54
00:05:39,958 --> 00:05:41,417
It'll cool down later.

55
00:05:42,625 --> 00:05:44,000
I almost didn't recognize you.

56
00:05:45,875 --> 00:05:47,208
Neither did I.

57
00:05:49,000 --> 00:05:50,000
[Martina laughs]

58
00:05:53,167 --> 00:05:55,292
No... It can't be.

59
00:05:56,375 --> 00:05:57,583
[man laughs]

60
00:05:59,958 --> 00:06:01,292
Sorry.

61
00:06:01,375 --> 00:06:03,042
- [man] No, no, it was...
- [Martina] Sorry.

62
00:06:03,125 --> 00:06:04,667
It was a long time ago.

63
00:06:04,750 --> 00:06:06,125
Twenty-five years.

64
00:06:06,208 --> 00:06:07,958
Twenty-five years without seeing each other.

65
00:06:09,417 --> 00:06:10,792
And we run into each other here, of all places.

66
00:06:10,875 --> 00:06:12,000
Well, I live here.

67
00:06:12,083 --> 00:06:14,125
No way! You've built your life here?

68
00:06:14,208 --> 00:06:15,917
No... [hesitates]

69
00:06:16,000 --> 00:06:18,750
If you... Well, I've been building it here. Yes.

70
00:06:18,958 --> 00:06:21,167
But I've done a lot over the years.

71
00:06:21,417 --> 00:06:22,792
It's like... Well, I don't know.

72
00:06:22,875 --> 00:06:24,208
No, there's no point talking about it.

73
00:06:24,292 --> 00:06:25,875
- [Martina] Better not, I don't know.
- [man] No, yes.

74
00:06:25,958 --> 00:06:27,292
Like you said, it's...

75
00:06:27,792 --> 00:06:29,000
...better not to talk about it.

76
00:06:29,958 --> 00:06:32,042
I'm running late. I have to cook for...

77
00:06:33,375 --> 00:06:35,000
...my husband, my family...

78
00:06:36,375 --> 00:06:38,500
Oh, no! Lucio, stop it.

79
00:06:38,583 --> 00:06:40,792
Sorry, we shouldn't talk about it.

80
00:06:41,042 --> 00:06:42,708
Well, did you have to bring it up?

81
00:06:42,958 --> 00:06:44,292
- [Martina] Why?
- [Lucio] You just had to!

82
00:06:44,375 --> 00:06:45,708
I know you, Martina.

83
00:06:45,792 --> 00:06:47,833
Just because I haven't heard from you doesn't
mean I don't know you.

84
00:06:47,917 --> 00:06:49,625
For instance, I know you're nervous.

85
00:06:49,917 --> 00:06:51,500
Here I am, standing in front of you,

86
00:06:51,583 --> 00:06:53,333
twenty-five years later,

87
00:06:53,417 --> 00:06:55,917
and all you can think to tell me is that you're going to

88
00:06:56,000 --> 00:06:58,125
- [Lucio] cook for...
- [Martina] My husband and daughter. Yes.

89
00:06:58,208 --> 00:06:59,292
There it is!

90
00:06:59,833 --> 00:07:01,833
Now I know everything about your life, don't I?

91
00:07:02,167 --> 00:07:04,083
Well... What did you want me to do, Lucio?

92
00:07:08,500 --> 00:07:09,917
I waited for you.

93
00:07:11,333 --> 00:07:12,958
You waited for me?

94
00:07:16,250 --> 00:07:17,375
[Lucio] Wha...?

95
00:07:17,458 --> 00:07:18,958
[Lucio] Your face! Are you kidding?

96
00:07:19,042 --> 00:07:20,667
Imagine how pathetic that would be...

97
00:07:21,000 --> 00:07:22,750
Some guy who never moved on because he was waiting

98
00:07:22,833 --> 00:07:24,708
for his teenage sweetheart. Give me a break!

99
00:07:24,792 --> 00:07:26,250
We weren't teenagers, Lucio.

100
00:07:26,333 --> 00:07:29,292
We acted like teenagers, but we weren't teenagers.

101
00:07:29,375 --> 00:07:31,667
- [Lucio] Those were good years, Martina.
- [Martina] Yes.

102
00:07:32,083 --> 00:07:33,583
Maybe the best years of my life.

103
00:07:33,708 --> 00:07:34,958
- [Martina] Really?
- [Lucio] Yes.

104
00:07:35,042 --> 00:07:37,250
[Lucio] That's why I was so happy to see you, Martina.

105
00:07:38,125 --> 00:07:39,875
Well, I have to go. I need to get to the airport.

106
00:07:39,958 --> 00:07:41,125
Oh, you're leaving already?

107
00:07:41,208 --> 00:07:42,625
No, I'm going to pick up my wife.

108
00:07:42,708 --> 00:07:44,125
Oh, ha, ha...

109
00:07:44,208 --> 00:07:46,625
Look who's dying to tell me that!

110
00:07:46,708 --> 00:07:49,083
I want her to see San Miguel. You know how fond I am of it.

111
00:07:49,167 --> 00:07:51,250
Yes, I remember perfectly.

112
00:07:52,167 --> 00:07:53,792
And on Monday we're heading back to Madrid.

113
00:07:54,000 --> 00:07:55,500
Lucio! Is she Spanish?

114
00:07:56,000 --> 00:07:57,583
I can't believe it!

115
00:07:57,667 --> 00:07:59,542
You always said that if you didn't marry me,

116
00:07:59,625 --> 00:08:00,833
you'd marry a Spanish woman.

117
00:08:00,917 --> 00:08:03,292
- [Martina] I can't believe it.
- [Lucio] See how well we know each other?

118
00:08:03,375 --> 00:08:04,875
We should exchange phone numbers,

119
00:08:04,958 --> 00:08:06,917
in case we ever forget something about each other.

120
00:08:07,000 --> 00:08:09,083
Oh, no, Lucio! Please spare me that.

121
00:08:09,167 --> 00:08:10,417
Of forgetting.

122
00:08:11,833 --> 00:08:12,958
Sorry for laughing.

123
00:08:13,042 --> 00:08:14,292
It's completely ridiculous.

124
00:08:14,958 --> 00:08:16,125
- [Martina] Hey...
- [Lucio] Hey... No, no.

125
00:08:16,208 --> 00:08:18,417
- [Lucio] You go ahead.
- [Martina] It's nothing, just...

126
00:08:18,500 --> 00:08:21,083
- [Martina] Tonight, at the theater...
- [Lucio] It's Florentina's thing.

127
00:08:21,500 --> 00:08:23,292
- [Lucio] Yes, we'll be there.
- [Martina] Really?

128
00:08:23,375 --> 00:08:24,667
That's great!

129
00:08:24,833 --> 00:08:26,292
Martina, can I ask you a favor?

130
00:08:26,583 --> 00:08:28,917
Let's not bring up our past, because I
haven't told her about you.

131
00:08:29,000 --> 00:08:30,375
I wouldn't want her to...

132
00:08:30,458 --> 00:08:32,958
Oh, Lucio! Please!

133
00:08:33,542 --> 00:08:35,125
My family doesn't even know who you are.

134
00:08:35,208 --> 00:08:36,750
They don't even know you exist.

135
00:08:36,917 --> 00:08:38,250
Don't worry.

136
00:08:39,958 --> 00:08:41,708
- [Martina] See you tonight.
- [Lucio] Bye.

137
00:08:41,792 --> 00:08:42,917
♪ Music begins ♪

138
00:08:44,000 --> 00:08:46,000
[woman] Ninety-nine, fifty-seven, thirty-two.

139
00:08:46,167 --> 00:08:47,417
[young man] Present.

140
00:08:47,625 --> 00:08:49,750
Six, six, nine, six, six, four.

141
00:08:49,833 --> 00:08:50,917
[girl] Present.

142
00:08:51,000 --> 00:08:53,167
Ninety-five, fifty-five, twenty-nine.

143
00:08:53,792 --> 00:08:55,042
[young man] Lucio!

144
00:08:55,417 --> 00:08:58,208
[teacher] Excuse me, are you 95, 55, 29?

145
00:08:58,292 --> 00:09:01,250
Yes, but I'd prefer you called me Lucio.

146
00:09:01,875 --> 00:09:04,208
[teacher] Nine, nine, six, four, four, zero.

147
00:09:04,625 --> 00:09:05,625
[young woman] Present.

148
00:09:05,708 --> 00:09:07,375
[teacher] Eighty-eight, thirty-three, zero, nine.

149
00:09:07,458 --> 00:09:08,500
[young man] Present.

150
00:09:08,750 --> 00:09:10,500
[teacher] Sixty-six, thirty, thirty.

151
00:09:10,583 --> 00:09:11,583
[girl] Present.

152
00:09:12,000 --> 00:09:13,333
♪ Music continues ♪

153
00:09:13,417 --> 00:09:15,417
[professor] Guys! A new and final

154
00:09:15,500 --> 00:09:17,083
ballet class time slot has just opened up.

155
00:09:17,625 --> 00:09:19,083
- [professor] Hello.
- [girl] Hello.

156
00:09:19,167 --> 00:09:20,167
Hey, my pen.

157
00:09:20,250 --> 00:09:21,333
Ame, what's your student ID number?

158
00:09:21,417 --> 00:09:22,417
[Amelia] Six, six, nine, six, six, four.

159
00:09:22,500 --> 00:09:24,208
- [girl] Hi, Ame.
- [boy] Hey, what's your name?

160
00:09:24,292 --> 00:09:25,458
♪ Music continues ♪

161
00:09:25,542 --> 00:09:27,667
Ninety-five, fifty-seven, twenty-one.

162
00:09:29,458 --> 00:09:31,458
Hey, what's your name? My pen!

163
00:09:37,667 --> 00:09:39,208
♪ Music continues ♪

164
00:09:50,458 --> 00:09:52,125
♪ Music ends ♪

165
00:09:54,125 --> 00:09:55,333
[Martina sips]

166
00:10:01,292 --> 00:10:02,542
[telephone rings]

167
00:10:05,333 --> 00:10:06,333
Hello...

168
00:10:06,417 --> 00:10:07,750
[Martina] Beatriz!

169
00:10:09,750 --> 00:10:11,125
I can't believe it.

170
00:10:11,708 --> 00:10:13,625
[Martina] Beatriz! Can you hear me?

171
00:10:14,792 --> 00:10:16,125
[Beatriz] Are you sick?

172
00:10:16,958 --> 00:10:19,000
I don't understand you, Beatriz.

173
00:10:19,083 --> 00:10:20,417
Why are you calling me?

174
00:10:21,125 --> 00:10:23,083
[Martina] Because I need to ask you a favor.

175
00:10:23,167 --> 00:10:24,708
♪ String music begins ♪

176
00:10:25,833 --> 00:10:27,625
[Martina] No, please. Don't cry.

177
00:10:27,917 --> 00:10:29,917
Look, do you want me to forgive you or not?

178
00:10:31,208 --> 00:10:33,250
Well, this is your big chance.

179
00:10:33,708 --> 00:10:35,208
[Beatriz] Oh, Martina! I've spent my whole life

180
00:10:35,292 --> 00:10:38,250
asking for your forgiveness, and right now
I'm the one who should be angry.

181
00:10:38,417 --> 00:10:40,542
[Martina] No, don't turn this around on me, please.

182
00:10:41,333 --> 00:10:42,542
I'm a widow!

183
00:10:42,625 --> 00:10:43,667
♪ Music continues ♪

184
00:10:43,750 --> 00:10:46,250
My Enrique Pérez Torres died!

185
00:10:46,333 --> 00:10:47,708
And you couldn't even be bothered to call me,

186
00:10:47,792 --> 00:10:49,708
to send me flowers,

187
00:10:49,792 --> 00:10:51,208
or a little card.

188
00:10:51,292 --> 00:10:52,542
[Martina] I pray for him every day,

189
00:10:52,625 --> 00:10:55,042
and I had a novena said for him, all right? For God's sake!

190
00:10:55,125 --> 00:10:56,542
[Beatriz] And what do you want from me now?

191
00:10:57,000 --> 00:10:58,292
[Martina] I want you to pack your bags

192
00:10:58,375 --> 00:11:00,417
and come spend a few days with me, you and Enriqueta.

193
00:11:00,500 --> 00:11:03,083
Well, Enriqueta has to come. That's the important thing.

194
00:11:03,167 --> 00:11:04,917
And I need you here right away.

195
00:11:05,042 --> 00:11:06,250
♪ Music continues ♪

196
00:11:06,333 --> 00:11:08,333
Can you tell me what's going on?

197
00:11:09,083 --> 00:11:10,750
I just ran into Lucio.

198
00:11:11,500 --> 00:11:12,833
[Martina] I know, I know,

199
00:11:12,917 --> 00:11:14,500
and I made up

200
00:11:14,583 --> 00:11:15,917
a life I don't have.

201
00:11:16,250 --> 00:11:17,917
I told him all sorts of things, and

202
00:11:18,000 --> 00:11:19,458
tonight

203
00:11:19,708 --> 00:11:21,333
we'll run into each other at the theater.

204
00:11:21,417 --> 00:11:22,958
Like a chance encounter,

205
00:11:23,042 --> 00:11:24,417
and I need to keep the story going.

206
00:11:24,500 --> 00:11:25,875
What did you tell him?

207
00:11:25,958 --> 00:11:27,333
♪ Music continues ♪

208
00:11:27,417 --> 00:11:29,833
[Martina] That I'd gotten married, had a daughter, and was happy.

209
00:11:30,458 --> 00:11:31,500
You lied about everything.

210
00:11:31,583 --> 00:11:32,833
No, not about the last part.

211
00:11:33,583 --> 00:11:34,958
But anyway, the point is that Enriqueta

212
00:11:35,042 --> 00:11:37,750
is the only girl I can trust, and she's family, Beatriz.

213
00:11:39,375 --> 00:11:40,458
♪ Music continues ♪

214
00:11:42,583 --> 00:11:44,167
Well, yes, I suppose...

215
00:11:45,292 --> 00:11:47,333
All right, you can borrow her.

216
00:11:48,083 --> 00:11:49,333
You can count on it.

217
00:11:49,417 --> 00:11:52,292
[Beatriz] But I can't provide the husband, you know.

218
00:11:52,375 --> 00:11:54,500
No, don't worry about that. I'll take care of the husband.

219
00:11:54,583 --> 00:11:56,917
What I need is for you to get here now, please!

220
00:11:57,458 --> 00:11:59,083
♪ Music changes to organ ♪

221
00:12:07,042 --> 00:12:09,042
[footsteps]

222
00:12:11,250 --> 00:12:12,250
Igor!

223
00:12:12,333 --> 00:12:13,667
♪ Organ music ends ♪

224
00:12:14,375 --> 00:12:15,542
[Martina] Give me the gun.

225
00:12:16,542 --> 00:12:17,875
[Martina] I said give me the gun.

226
00:12:18,583 --> 00:12:19,917
Give me the gun.

227
00:12:20,458 --> 00:12:21,542
[Igor] Sorry, Martina.

228
00:12:21,625 --> 00:12:23,792
No, I've already told you, not in my house, Igor.

229
00:12:23,875 --> 00:12:25,833
You'll get me into trouble, and I've got plenty already.

230
00:12:26,583 --> 00:12:29,458
Look at you. Even a whole bottle can't give you the courage.

231
00:12:29,542 --> 00:12:32,625
How many times have you pointed that thing at
yourself without pulling the trigger, you
coward?

232
00:12:32,708 --> 00:12:34,875
They're pressuring me to finish the story.

233
00:12:34,958 --> 00:12:36,125
Then finish it, period.

234
00:12:36,208 --> 00:12:37,792
How many times, Martina?

235
00:12:38,208 --> 00:12:40,500
How many more stories are they going to steal from me?

236
00:12:40,583 --> 00:12:42,917
As many as you let them. You have to put a stop to it.

237
00:12:43,000 --> 00:12:44,083
They'd throw me in jail.

238
00:12:44,167 --> 00:12:46,042
No, no. Jail is out of the question right now.

239
00:12:46,708 --> 00:12:48,708
Look at this mess you've made of my house.

240
00:12:49,375 --> 00:12:50,750
Look, Igor...

241
00:12:52,292 --> 00:12:53,792
...you have to do yourself a favor.

242
00:12:53,875 --> 00:12:56,250
- [Igor] Shoot myself?
- [Martina] No, no, no!

243
00:12:56,708 --> 00:12:57,875
Look at me.

244
00:12:59,542 --> 00:13:00,917
You need to take a bath,

245
00:13:01,500 --> 00:13:02,583
shave,

246
00:13:03,333 --> 00:13:04,333
and stop drinking.

247
00:13:05,500 --> 00:13:07,417
I want you to come to the theater with me tonight.

248
00:13:07,500 --> 00:13:09,042
You've got to be kidding. The theater? How?

249
00:13:09,125 --> 00:13:10,292
I have to finish writing!

250
00:13:10,375 --> 00:13:12,167
Otherwise... otherwise the payment gets delayed.

251
00:13:12,250 --> 00:13:14,833
How am I supposed to pay you? Tell me! How will I pay you?

252
00:13:14,917 --> 00:13:16,542
I'll let you have two months' rent free.

253
00:13:17,458 --> 00:13:19,167
[Martina] I'll explain once you're sober.

254
00:13:19,250 --> 00:13:20,625
I can't...

255
00:13:20,875 --> 00:13:22,125
No, I can't.

256
00:13:23,000 --> 00:13:24,000
Please!

257
00:13:24,292 --> 00:13:25,667
No, no, I can't.

258
00:13:26,667 --> 00:13:28,458
[Igor] I can't, I can't.

259
00:13:28,542 --> 00:13:30,458
I'll even give you a whole year rent-free.

260
00:13:34,250 --> 00:13:35,583
♪ Music begins ♪

261
00:13:35,958 --> 00:13:37,083
[Martina] Drunk.

262
00:13:38,708 --> 00:13:40,292
[airplane engine]

263
00:13:48,042 --> 00:13:49,375
♪ Music continues ♪

264
00:13:56,667 --> 00:13:58,125
♪ Music ends ♪

265
00:13:58,250 --> 00:13:59,417
[Lucio] My goodness.

266
00:13:59,500 --> 00:14:00,875
[Lucio] Everything okay?

267
00:14:02,208 --> 00:14:03,542
I asked if everything's okay.

268
00:14:03,625 --> 00:14:05,500
[woman] Everything's going splendidly.

269
00:14:05,750 --> 00:14:08,250
I just love throwing up every time I arrive in a new city!

270
00:14:08,667 --> 00:14:10,250
Oh, it's good luck!

271
00:14:10,500 --> 00:14:11,833
[woman] What an asshole.

272
00:14:11,917 --> 00:14:13,292
Oh, I feel so sick!

273
00:14:13,500 --> 00:14:16,250
Sorry, darling! You should have come by road.

274
00:14:16,333 --> 00:14:17,750
The flight was already paid for.

275
00:14:17,833 --> 00:14:20,125
And with the outrageous prices they charge for these services...

276
00:14:20,208 --> 00:14:22,167
Honestly, it's like paying for a flight back to Madrid.

277
00:14:22,250 --> 00:14:23,333
[engine stops]

278
00:14:23,417 --> 00:14:24,542
It's the truth.

279
00:14:24,625 --> 00:14:25,917
The good thing is you're here now.

280
00:14:26,000 --> 00:14:27,667
[Lucio] I needed you to get here. I have something to tell you.

281
00:14:27,750 --> 00:14:29,042
So do we.

282
00:14:29,125 --> 00:14:31,250
Darling, you can spare me the kiss.

283
00:14:31,375 --> 00:14:33,208
Just put my luggage in the trunk.

284
00:14:33,292 --> 00:14:34,833
I need to recover.

285
00:14:34,917 --> 00:14:36,167
[Lucio] Oh, Vicente called.

286
00:14:36,250 --> 00:14:37,708
He just hit the road.

287
00:14:38,000 --> 00:14:40,000
Sir, open the door for me, please.

288
00:14:40,083 --> 00:14:42,708
I told him we'd go ahead to the hotel for a bite to eat

289
00:14:42,792 --> 00:14:44,333
and a shower before the theater.

290
00:14:45,167 --> 00:14:47,167
[woman] When do you think he'll arrive?

291
00:14:47,417 --> 00:14:48,917
In about two or three hours.

292
00:14:49,792 --> 00:14:50,792
Thank you.

293
00:14:50,875 --> 00:14:52,542
[woman] Might as well get it over with.

294
00:14:52,667 --> 00:14:54,417
♪ Music begins ♪

295
00:14:58,500 --> 00:14:59,708
[Lucio] Need a hand, darling?

296
00:14:59,792 --> 00:15:01,625
I'm dizzy, for fuck's sake, not paralyzed.

297
00:15:01,708 --> 00:15:03,833
♪ You've got poison in your skin ♪

298
00:15:03,917 --> 00:15:04,958
[buzzer]

299
00:15:05,042 --> 00:15:07,958
♪ Because you're made of fine plastic ♪

300
00:15:08,042 --> 00:15:11,250
♪ They say your touch is divine ♪

301
00:15:11,500 --> 00:15:13,917
♪ And whoever touches you is drawn in ♪

302
00:15:14,000 --> 00:15:15,417
[hall monitor] Your skirt, miss!

303
00:15:15,500 --> 00:15:18,042
♪ And if you want to go dancing tonight ♪

304
00:15:18,375 --> 00:15:21,708
♪ Start putting on your sinner's costume ♪

305
00:15:21,792 --> 00:15:24,875
♪ But you'll have to be ready in half an hour ♪

306
00:15:25,208 --> 00:15:27,875
♪ Otherwise I won't come pick you up ♪

307
00:15:28,542 --> 00:15:30,917
♪ But first you want to go out to dinner... ♪

308
00:15:31,000 --> 00:15:32,000
[clapping]

309
00:15:32,083 --> 00:15:34,583
[teacher] Get ready. We're about to begin.

310
00:15:35,583 --> 00:15:37,500
♪ Let's see if they accept unemployment papers... ♪

311
00:15:37,583 --> 00:15:38,792
Good morning, Martina.

312
00:15:38,875 --> 00:15:40,125
[Martina] Good morning.

313
00:15:40,792 --> 00:15:41,792
[clapping]

314
00:15:42,833 --> 00:15:45,375
[teacher] Please put your things in your lockers.

315
00:15:45,917 --> 00:15:47,042
[teacher] And take your places

316
00:15:47,125 --> 00:15:49,833
where you can see yourselves in the mirror during practice.

317
00:15:49,917 --> 00:15:50,917
♪ Music ends ♪

318
00:15:51,000 --> 00:15:53,625
[Martina] Ninety-five, fifty-five, twenty-nine!

319
00:15:53,833 --> 00:15:55,833
Lucio! I prefer to be called Lucio.

320
00:15:56,375 --> 00:15:57,708
And what's your name?

321
00:15:57,958 --> 00:15:59,292
[Amelia] Martina, come here!

322
00:15:59,583 --> 00:16:00,583
[clapping]

323
00:16:00,875 --> 00:16:02,333
[teacher] Everyone, take your places!

324
00:16:02,750 --> 00:16:04,875
Welcome to your first day of class!

325
00:16:05,250 --> 00:16:06,500
Martina!

326
00:16:07,250 --> 00:16:08,958
[Lucio] Hey, that's a great name.

327
00:16:10,917 --> 00:16:13,375
[teacher] Majo, Karime, please take your places.

328
00:16:16,167 --> 00:16:18,000
[teacher] Are you sure you're in the right room?

329
00:16:18,875 --> 00:16:19,958
Yes.

330
00:16:20,583 --> 00:16:21,667
[teacher] Welcome.

331
00:16:22,458 --> 00:16:23,667
Get ready...

332
00:16:24,708 --> 00:16:27,458
Five, six, seven, eight.

333
00:16:28,167 --> 00:16:29,208
Plié.

334
00:16:29,333 --> 00:16:30,792
♪ Classical music begins ♪

335
00:16:32,000 --> 00:16:33,000
Plié.

336
00:16:37,125 --> 00:16:38,333
Grand plié.

337
00:16:40,917 --> 00:16:41,917
♪ Music continues ♪

338
00:16:44,167 --> 00:16:45,333
Ramasser.

339
00:16:52,542 --> 00:16:53,667
Cambré.

340
00:16:55,208 --> 00:16:56,208
♪ Music continues ♪

341
00:16:57,125 --> 00:16:58,542
[clock hands ticking]

342
00:17:03,375 --> 00:17:04,417
Bow.

343
00:17:07,500 --> 00:17:09,042
♪ Music continues ♪

344
00:17:11,125 --> 00:17:13,292
[teacher] Welcome to the new school year.

345
00:17:13,375 --> 00:17:14,708
[laughter]

346
00:17:15,167 --> 00:17:17,625
- [teacher] Sorry, I'm used to saying that.
- [Lucio] No problem.

347
00:17:18,042 --> 00:17:20,708
[teacher] To be honest, we don't have a great dancer here.

348
00:17:20,792 --> 00:17:22,292
But we do have a brave man.

349
00:17:22,625 --> 00:17:24,625
So, welcome, everyone!

350
00:17:24,708 --> 00:17:26,042
♪ Classical music ends ♪

351
00:17:28,083 --> 00:17:30,417
If he likes ballet, I don't think you're his type.

352
00:17:31,583 --> 00:17:32,958
He's here because of me.

353
00:17:34,375 --> 00:17:35,917
♪ Music begins ♪

354
00:17:40,917 --> 00:17:42,167
[Martina] There he is!

355
00:17:42,250 --> 00:17:43,958
There he is, there he is, there he is.

356
00:17:45,042 --> 00:17:47,125
[Amelia] An apple and a pear, please.

357
00:17:49,667 --> 00:17:51,167
♪ Music ends ♪

358
00:17:54,083 --> 00:17:55,708
[Martina] Hey! Can we sit here?

359
00:17:56,250 --> 00:17:58,875
- [Lucio] Yes.
- [Amelia] So, you're into ballet?

360
00:17:58,958 --> 00:17:59,958
Yes, why?

361
00:18:00,042 --> 00:18:01,500
Because you're pretty bad at it, aren't you?

362
00:18:01,583 --> 00:18:02,833
[Martina] He can learn.

363
00:18:03,833 --> 00:18:05,042
You can learn.

364
00:18:05,500 --> 00:18:07,208
I prefer another kind of dance.

365
00:18:08,042 --> 00:18:09,208
Really? Which kind?

366
00:18:09,292 --> 00:18:10,417
Contemporary dance.

367
00:18:12,000 --> 00:18:13,625
So why did you sign up for ballet?

368
00:18:13,875 --> 00:18:15,875
Because there weren't any contemporary dance classes.

369
00:18:16,958 --> 00:18:18,417
You wanted to spend more time with me!

370
00:18:18,500 --> 00:18:20,083
[Amelia] Martina! Shut up!

371
00:18:22,042 --> 00:18:23,250
Well, it's true.

372
00:18:23,333 --> 00:18:24,958
♪ Music begins ♪

373
00:18:27,583 --> 00:18:29,125
[buzzer]

374
00:18:36,417 --> 00:18:38,333
I've had enough sweets. We're leaving.

375
00:18:38,417 --> 00:18:40,042
No, we're not going back inside.

376
00:18:40,375 --> 00:18:41,500
[Amelia] Yes, we are.

377
00:18:41,583 --> 00:18:42,875
[Martina] We're not.

378
00:18:43,000 --> 00:18:44,375
I'm going to grant him a wish.

379
00:18:44,875 --> 00:18:46,250
- [Martina] Come on.
- [Lucio] But wait...

380
00:18:47,333 --> 00:18:48,542
[Amelia] Martina!

381
00:18:48,667 --> 00:18:50,417
What? Martina, where are you going?

382
00:18:50,500 --> 00:18:52,000
Martina, you don't even know him!

383
00:18:52,125 --> 00:18:53,458
♪ Music continues ♪

384
00:19:02,208 --> 00:19:03,292
[Martina] Run!

385
00:19:04,292 --> 00:19:05,375
♪ Music continues ♪

386
00:19:05,458 --> 00:19:07,125
[hall monitor] Young people, stop!

387
00:19:07,208 --> 00:19:08,417
Please, stop!

388
00:19:08,833 --> 00:19:09,833
[Martina] Run!

389
00:19:10,250 --> 00:19:11,667
- [hall monitor] Young man, young lady!
- [Martina] Run, run!

390
00:19:11,750 --> 00:19:13,042
[hall monitor] I'm talking to you!

391
00:19:13,583 --> 00:19:15,000
Please, you two!

392
00:19:15,958 --> 00:19:19,875
♪ Somewhere in a big country ♪

393
00:19:22,333 --> 00:19:25,000
♪ They forgot to build... ♪

394
00:19:25,083 --> 00:19:27,750
[Martina] That's when I found out Lucio
didn't know the city very well.

395
00:19:28,042 --> 00:19:29,667
And I'd always thought I could be

396
00:19:29,750 --> 00:19:31,333
a great tour guide.

397
00:19:32,625 --> 00:19:34,542
And, well, I was much braver than he was.

398
00:19:34,625 --> 00:19:36,250
Or at least that's how it seemed.

399
00:19:36,917 --> 00:19:38,958
Then he explained to me

400
00:19:39,042 --> 00:19:41,167
that women mature earlier than men.

401
00:19:42,000 --> 00:19:43,458
So it was already written.

402
00:19:44,417 --> 00:19:46,750
It was the law of life, whether we liked it or not.

403
00:19:46,833 --> 00:19:47,833
[Igor groans]

404
00:19:47,917 --> 00:19:49,208
Oh, sorry. Excuse me.

405
00:19:49,292 --> 00:19:50,875
Look... It's nothing, okay?

406
00:19:50,958 --> 00:19:51,958
♪ Music continues ♪

407
00:19:52,042 --> 00:19:53,042
Should I keep going?

408
00:19:53,125 --> 00:19:54,250
No, no, I'll finish it.

409
00:19:54,333 --> 00:19:56,083
No! I mean should I keep telling the story?

410
00:19:56,167 --> 00:19:57,292
Am I boring you?

411
00:19:57,917 --> 00:19:58,917
Go on...

412
00:20:00,250 --> 00:20:01,792
So we ended up on

413
00:20:02,000 --> 00:20:04,083
the balcony of my favorite building.

414
00:20:05,167 --> 00:20:08,125
[Martina] We decided we'd only ask each other ten questions.

415
00:20:08,500 --> 00:20:09,917
And we wouldn't question each other again,

416
00:20:10,000 --> 00:20:11,375
so we could discover who we were together.

417
00:20:11,458 --> 00:20:12,458
♪ Music ends ♪

418
00:20:12,542 --> 00:20:13,708
[Lucio] One!

419
00:20:14,083 --> 00:20:16,083
My name is Lucio Leal Fernández.

420
00:20:16,167 --> 00:20:18,083
[Martina] I'm Martina Jiménez Torres.

421
00:20:18,792 --> 00:20:19,958
Two!

422
00:20:20,500 --> 00:20:21,500
I'm seventeen.

423
00:20:21,583 --> 00:20:22,958
[Lucio] I'm younger than you.

424
00:20:23,042 --> 00:20:24,708
- [Martina] How old?
- [Lucio] Sixteen.

425
00:20:24,875 --> 00:20:25,875
[Lucio] Four!

426
00:20:25,958 --> 00:20:28,125
- [Martina] We were on three.
- [Lucio] Three was: "How old?"

427
00:20:29,500 --> 00:20:31,125
[Martina] Okay. Four!

428
00:20:31,833 --> 00:20:33,333
My family consists of

429
00:20:33,417 --> 00:20:35,083
my dad Martín, my mom Hilda,

430
00:20:35,167 --> 00:20:36,333
and my sister Beatriz.

431
00:20:36,417 --> 00:20:38,125
My family is my father Augusto

432
00:20:38,208 --> 00:20:39,750
and my dog Camilo Cienfuegos.

433
00:20:40,833 --> 00:20:42,708
Five! And your mother?

434
00:20:43,125 --> 00:20:44,458
She's dead.

435
00:20:44,833 --> 00:20:45,833
In heaven?

436
00:20:46,125 --> 00:20:47,250
No, she's dead.

437
00:20:48,167 --> 00:20:49,333
You don't have a religion?

438
00:20:49,667 --> 00:20:50,667
No.

439
00:20:50,958 --> 00:20:53,000
I was taught to believe that if you do good things,

440
00:20:53,083 --> 00:20:54,458
good things will come to you.

441
00:20:55,792 --> 00:20:56,917
I'm Catholic.

442
00:20:57,750 --> 00:20:59,042
My family is very religious.

443
00:20:59,125 --> 00:21:01,792
So they taught me to believe that if I do bad things,

444
00:21:02,417 --> 00:21:04,458
I can go to church and have God forgive me

445
00:21:04,958 --> 00:21:06,958
and not take responsibility for my actions.

446
00:21:08,583 --> 00:21:10,458
Who's the person you trust the most?

447
00:21:10,792 --> 00:21:12,250
Amelia.

448
00:21:13,042 --> 00:21:15,042
If I were a lesbian, she'd be my girlfriend.

449
00:21:15,833 --> 00:21:16,833
What about you?

450
00:21:16,917 --> 00:21:18,417
Camilo Cienfuegos.

451
00:21:18,500 --> 00:21:20,625
If I were a dog, I'd be his bitch.

452
00:21:25,208 --> 00:21:27,083
I'm afraid of people who lie.

453
00:21:28,042 --> 00:21:29,375
People who are disloyal.

454
00:21:29,625 --> 00:21:31,000
My last name is Leal. It means loyal.

455
00:21:34,917 --> 00:21:36,583
I'm afraid of heights.

456
00:21:36,667 --> 00:21:38,208
If I'm here with you,

457
00:21:38,292 --> 00:21:40,125
it's because I trust you.

458
00:21:44,250 --> 00:21:45,542
Ten!

459
00:21:46,208 --> 00:21:47,208
I'm a virgin.

460
00:21:47,542 --> 00:21:48,667
I'm a virgin.

461
00:21:53,042 --> 00:21:54,042
Bonus question!

462
00:21:54,125 --> 00:21:56,125
Think carefully! This is the last one.

463
00:21:59,167 --> 00:22:00,792
What's your favorite song?

464
00:22:01,292 --> 00:22:02,708
You won't know it.

465
00:22:02,958 --> 00:22:03,958
It's by a Chilean band.

466
00:22:04,042 --> 00:22:05,375
Give me a chance.

467
00:22:05,917 --> 00:22:07,375
They're called Los Prisioneros.

468
00:22:07,625 --> 00:22:08,833
♪ Song begins ♪

469
00:22:08,917 --> 00:22:12,083
♪ Don't stand in front of me ♪

470
00:22:13,375 --> 00:22:17,750
♪ With that hurtful look ♪

471
00:22:17,833 --> 00:22:21,958
♪ I can understand narrow-mindedness ♪

472
00:22:22,208 --> 00:22:26,542
♪ Put up with inexperience ♪

473
00:22:26,750 --> 00:22:29,292
♪ But I won't tolerate ♪

474
00:22:29,375 --> 00:22:32,500
♪ A narrow heart! ♪

475
00:22:32,583 --> 00:22:34,417
♪ Song ends ♪
♪ Music begins ♪

476
00:22:47,125 --> 00:22:48,500
♪ Music continues ♪

477
00:23:00,583 --> 00:23:01,917
♪ Music continues ♪

478
00:23:07,208 --> 00:23:09,958
♪ Don't ever talk like that again ♪

479
00:23:10,750 --> 00:23:11,917
♪ Don't cheapen these relationships... ♪

480
00:23:12,000 --> 00:23:14,125
[Martina] My life slowly began to change.

481
00:23:14,417 --> 00:23:16,500
[Martina] I'm sure his did too.

482
00:23:16,583 --> 00:23:19,875
♪ Darling, don't tell me about that ♪

483
00:23:19,958 --> 00:23:21,875
♪ About hatred and betrayal ♪

484
00:23:21,958 --> 00:23:24,750
♪ How many things will be said? ♪

485
00:23:25,458 --> 00:23:28,708
♪ In the war of love ♪

486
00:23:28,917 --> 00:23:31,750
♪ Words are knives ♪

487
00:23:31,833 --> 00:23:35,000
♪ When pride and passion wield them... ♪

488
00:23:35,083 --> 00:23:37,042
Up, relevé.

489
00:23:37,125 --> 00:23:42,750
♪ You're crying and doing nothing ♪

490
00:23:44,167 --> 00:23:47,250
♪ To understand anyone ♪

491
00:23:47,333 --> 00:23:50,583
♪ But yourself ♪

492
00:23:50,708 --> 00:23:54,292
♪ Hey, I won't put up with it ♪

493
00:23:54,375 --> 00:23:57,625
♪ You can't prove it ♪

494
00:23:58,042 --> 00:24:00,708
♪ Hey, I won't put up with it ♪

495
00:24:00,792 --> 00:24:03,958
♪ A narrow heart ♪

496
00:24:04,125 --> 00:24:06,000
[teacher] ...we studied nature and matter,

497
00:24:06,083 --> 00:24:08,208
some of the most characteristic atomic properties,

498
00:24:08,292 --> 00:24:10,333
- such as...
- [Amelia] Hey!

499
00:24:10,417 --> 00:24:12,417
[teacher] ...ionization energy

500
00:24:12,917 --> 00:24:14,542
and atomic radius.

501
00:24:15,375 --> 00:24:16,542
[teacher] However,

502
00:24:16,625 --> 00:24:19,625
these are characteristics of neutral, isolated atoms.

503
00:24:20,708 --> 00:24:23,083
[teacher] That is, monatomic substances,

504
00:24:23,375 --> 00:24:25,750
- but reality, by nature...
- [Martina] Lucio.

505
00:24:26,167 --> 00:24:28,208
[teacher] With the exception of noble gases,

506
00:24:28,292 --> 00:24:30,458
which are monatomic,

507
00:24:30,583 --> 00:24:33,000
all the other elements are...

508
00:24:34,083 --> 00:24:40,000
♪ You know how much love there's been ♪

509
00:24:41,292 --> 00:24:47,208
♪ You've embraced the same things I have ♪

510
00:24:47,750 --> 00:24:51,000
♪ Today you can't prove ♪

511
00:24:51,417 --> 00:24:54,708
♪ I don't have to put up with it ♪

512
00:24:54,958 --> 00:24:57,708
♪ No, you can't prove ♪

513
00:24:57,792 --> 00:25:01,000
♪ A narrow heart... ♪

514
00:25:02,667 --> 00:25:04,458
[Martina] Seek and you shall find.

515
00:25:04,542 --> 00:25:07,083
And just like that, suddenly, behind a mysterious door

516
00:25:07,417 --> 00:25:09,667
was what we would come to call

517
00:25:10,125 --> 00:25:12,333
the last corner of the world.

518
00:25:14,625 --> 00:25:17,458
♪ Your heart... ♪

519
00:25:17,792 --> 00:25:19,583
[Martina] It was love at first sight.

520
00:25:19,667 --> 00:25:22,542
[Martina] It was fun. Things were different there.

521
00:25:22,625 --> 00:25:24,333
♪ A narrow heart ♪

522
00:25:24,417 --> 00:25:25,792
♪ Music ends ♪

523
00:25:26,458 --> 00:25:27,917
[teacher] Bravo!

524
00:25:28,083 --> 00:25:30,375
You two, come over here!

525
00:25:31,750 --> 00:25:34,875
[Martina] That was the beginning of the
happiest years of my life.

526
00:25:35,750 --> 00:25:38,167
There are moments, Igor, that...

527
00:25:38,917 --> 00:25:41,042
...make this life worth living.

528
00:25:42,167 --> 00:25:43,417
Do you understand?

529
00:25:44,000 --> 00:25:45,000
[Igor snores]

530
00:25:50,000 --> 00:25:51,000
[Igor snores]

531
00:25:51,583 --> 00:25:53,125
[Lucio] Well, no, like an idiot!

532
00:25:53,208 --> 00:25:55,375
Like a moron, man. Like a little grade-school kid.

533
00:25:55,458 --> 00:25:56,750
I couldn't stop laughing.

534
00:25:57,208 --> 00:25:58,875
I looked like I was high, man.

535
00:25:59,500 --> 00:26:01,292
Man, I'd dreamed about that reunion thousands of times,

536
00:26:01,375 --> 00:26:02,625
and there I go, screwing it up!

537
00:26:02,708 --> 00:26:04,750
[man on phone] Are you serious?

538
00:26:04,833 --> 00:26:06,667
Holy shit! I was sure she was dead.

539
00:26:06,792 --> 00:26:08,083
Don't joke about that, man.

540
00:26:08,167 --> 00:26:09,958
Look, forget about the theater.

541
00:26:10,042 --> 00:26:11,833
Let's go to dinner. We haven't done that in ages.

542
00:26:11,917 --> 00:26:13,125
And we'll talk.

543
00:26:13,375 --> 00:26:15,042
All I can think about is seeing her again.

544
00:26:15,583 --> 00:26:17,667
Do you think I should tell Loles about it?

545
00:26:17,750 --> 00:26:20,083
I don't know... No, why?

546
00:26:20,250 --> 00:26:22,417
[Lucio] So she knows what's going to happen tonight, right?

547
00:26:23,292 --> 00:26:24,833
What's going to happen tonight?

548
00:26:24,958 --> 00:26:26,000
[knocking at door]

549
00:26:26,083 --> 00:26:28,500
- [Lucio] Who is it?
- [Loles] Loles, who else?

550
00:26:28,833 --> 00:26:29,833
[hesitates]

551
00:26:29,917 --> 00:26:30,958
Well, it's her. Hold on.

552
00:26:31,042 --> 00:26:32,667
- [man] Who's her?
- [Lucio] Coming!

553
00:26:33,958 --> 00:26:35,708
Come on, darling, why are we cooped up in here?

554
00:26:35,792 --> 00:26:37,250
Seriously! When it's so beautiful outside.

555
00:26:37,333 --> 00:26:38,750
Come on, let's go for a walk.

556
00:26:38,833 --> 00:26:40,417
It's Vicente. He's almost here.

557
00:26:40,708 --> 00:26:41,708
So?

558
00:26:42,000 --> 00:26:43,000
What's wrong?

559
00:26:43,167 --> 00:26:45,042
Oh! Do we have to wait for him just to go sightseeing too?

560
00:26:45,125 --> 00:26:47,125
What are you two up to, you little queers?

561
00:26:47,458 --> 00:26:49,333
Look, step on it. I'll see you here.

562
00:26:52,000 --> 00:26:53,417
[exhales]

563
00:26:55,708 --> 00:26:58,500
[car horn]

564
00:27:00,917 --> 00:27:03,167
Let me pass, you idiot!

565
00:27:03,708 --> 00:27:05,000
[engine revving]

566
00:27:06,917 --> 00:27:08,583
[Vicente] It had to be a woman driver!

567
00:27:08,667 --> 00:27:10,542
God's going to punish you, you know.

568
00:27:10,625 --> 00:27:11,917
Faggot!

569
00:27:12,000 --> 00:27:13,542
[Beatriz shushes] Sweetheart, please!

570
00:27:13,625 --> 00:27:15,208
[cell phone rings] It's Aunt Martina.

571
00:27:15,958 --> 00:27:17,708
Well, answer it. See what she wants.

572
00:27:20,667 --> 00:27:22,083
We're right here, Auntie!

573
00:27:22,250 --> 00:27:24,083
[Martina on phone] Oh, what a beautiful voice!

574
00:27:24,167 --> 00:27:25,208
You speak so clearly now.

575
00:27:25,292 --> 00:27:27,500
Auntie, I'm nine years old already.

576
00:27:27,792 --> 00:27:29,042
Let me talk to her.

577
00:27:29,125 --> 00:27:30,750
Hey, hey, hey!

578
00:27:32,083 --> 00:27:33,458
Haven't we heard anything from him?

579
00:27:34,208 --> 00:27:35,875
[Martina] You're curious to see him, aren't you?

580
00:27:36,083 --> 00:27:38,250
Absolutely not. You'll ruin everything.

581
00:27:38,333 --> 00:27:39,583
See you here.

582
00:27:40,958 --> 00:27:42,417
- [Enriqueta] Mom.
- [Beatriz] What?

583
00:27:42,500 --> 00:27:44,083
Who's "him"?

584
00:27:46,833 --> 00:27:49,042
Why has Aunt Martina never liked you?

585
00:27:50,625 --> 00:27:51,667
[Beatriz sighs]

586
00:27:51,750 --> 00:27:54,000
You used to love me, didn't you, Martina?

587
00:27:55,083 --> 00:27:56,500
I was her favorite sister.

588
00:27:56,833 --> 00:27:58,292
Well, you were her only sister.

589
00:27:58,375 --> 00:28:01,000
Yes, and he was the most handsome boy in school.

590
00:28:01,083 --> 00:28:02,208
He had the face of an angel.

591
00:28:04,667 --> 00:28:07,250
[Beatriz] But he was as wicked as he was handsome.

592
00:28:07,583 --> 00:28:08,708
Kiss Amelia.

593
00:28:08,875 --> 00:28:09,875
Why me?

594
00:28:09,958 --> 00:28:11,333
Because there are only three of us.

595
00:28:13,750 --> 00:28:15,417
[Beatriz] They did very strange things.

596
00:28:18,167 --> 00:28:19,583
Pass it to the right.

597
00:28:29,208 --> 00:28:31,500
[Enriqueta] You never played with them?

598
00:28:33,083 --> 00:28:34,250
Never!

599
00:28:34,333 --> 00:28:35,333
I don't believe you.

600
00:28:35,417 --> 00:28:36,458
What do you mean you don't believe me?

601
00:28:36,542 --> 00:28:38,125
Why don't you believe me? I'm your mother!

602
00:28:38,208 --> 00:28:40,792
Because nobody can be angry about people kissing!

603
00:28:41,000 --> 00:28:43,500
You kiss people you love!

604
00:28:43,667 --> 00:28:45,208
But they kissed on the mouth.

605
00:28:45,292 --> 00:28:47,833
- [Enriqueta] So what?
- [Beatriz] What do you mean, so what? Enriqueta!

606
00:28:48,250 --> 00:28:50,458
[Beatriz] A lot happened, Queta. So many things,

607
00:28:50,542 --> 00:28:52,833
so many things that even I didn't know about.

608
00:28:52,917 --> 00:28:54,792
And I only found out afterward.

609
00:28:54,875 --> 00:28:57,208
[Lucio] Nobody has to find out.

610
00:28:57,417 --> 00:28:59,417
It's at the last corner of the world.

611
00:29:01,208 --> 00:29:02,208
[Amelia] I just can't believe

612
00:29:02,292 --> 00:29:04,833
you agreed to share our place with a stranger!

613
00:29:04,917 --> 00:29:06,083
[Martina] It's not that we agreed.

614
00:29:06,167 --> 00:29:08,500
[Lucio] We suggested it. We can't do what we want over there...

615
00:29:08,583 --> 00:29:11,458
I don't want to rehearse with him! This was
supposed to be just the three of us.

616
00:29:11,542 --> 00:29:14,083
[Martina] You're not interested in dancing
anymore. That's different.

617
00:29:14,167 --> 00:29:16,083
Why don't you find something you actually like?

618
00:29:16,167 --> 00:29:17,958
We agreed no one would impose anything on anyone else.

619
00:29:18,042 --> 00:29:19,708
[Lucio] We live in a free republic.

620
00:29:19,792 --> 00:29:21,000
If you want another activity...

621
00:29:21,083 --> 00:29:22,500
Then we should find one.

622
00:29:22,583 --> 00:29:24,250
[Lucio] This is what we want to do.

623
00:29:25,000 --> 00:29:26,417
He wants something else.

624
00:29:26,500 --> 00:29:27,917
Who? Balthazar?

625
00:29:28,000 --> 00:29:29,833
- [Amelia] Yes.
- [Lucio] Are you jealous?

626
00:29:29,917 --> 00:29:32,333
- [Amelia] What would I be jealous of?
- [Lucio] Someone else coming in here.

627
00:29:32,417 --> 00:29:34,042
- [Martina] Beatriz has been here.
- [Amelia] That's not the same!

628
00:29:34,125 --> 00:29:36,542
- [Amelia] Beatriz is stupid!
- [Lucio] Don't be stupid yourself, Amelia.

629
00:29:36,625 --> 00:29:39,125
Look, I found this place, and I can put an end to it, okay?

630
00:29:40,500 --> 00:29:41,583
[Lucio] Amelia!

631
00:29:41,667 --> 00:29:44,042
- [Martina] I think I'd better go after her.
- [Lucio] She'll come back.

632
00:29:44,292 --> 00:29:45,417
Leave her alone.

633
00:29:46,208 --> 00:29:49,083
[Martina] You're as smart as those two are stupid.

634
00:29:50,042 --> 00:29:51,875
You wanted us to be alone, didn't you?

635
00:29:52,333 --> 00:29:54,125
Amelia will find something she likes.

636
00:29:54,875 --> 00:29:57,083
This place is for all of us to do what we want.

637
00:29:57,167 --> 00:29:58,875
And Amelia needs to understand that.

638
00:30:00,083 --> 00:30:01,875
It used to be just the two of us.

639
00:30:02,750 --> 00:30:04,500
So I'm to blame.

640
00:30:06,458 --> 00:30:08,333
My parents say I'm changing.

641
00:30:08,917 --> 00:30:10,375
Has your father said anything to you?

642
00:30:11,667 --> 00:30:14,083
Yesterday he said this country is going to hell

643
00:30:14,167 --> 00:30:15,625
and nobody is doing anything.

644
00:30:16,375 --> 00:30:18,792
They say we need solidarity. Just look around.

645
00:30:19,167 --> 00:30:20,958
But has he said anything about us?

646
00:30:21,042 --> 00:30:22,125
He doesn't know.

647
00:30:22,750 --> 00:30:24,125
This is between you and me.

648
00:30:25,792 --> 00:30:27,458
The teacher likes you.

649
00:30:28,000 --> 00:30:29,083
Balthazar?

650
00:30:29,167 --> 00:30:30,375
That's what Amelia was talking about.

651
00:30:30,458 --> 00:30:32,000
Why do you think he agreed to come here?

652
00:30:32,083 --> 00:30:33,583
We insisted.

653
00:30:34,125 --> 00:30:35,292
How would you feel?

654
00:30:36,417 --> 00:30:38,417
About what? Balthazar liking me?

655
00:30:39,417 --> 00:30:41,042
Well, I'd think that was nice.

656
00:30:41,375 --> 00:30:42,875
Are you serious?

657
00:30:43,167 --> 00:30:44,917
It's nice when someone likes you.

658
00:30:46,042 --> 00:30:47,917
- [Martina] What would you do?
- [Lucio] Nothing.

659
00:30:48,875 --> 00:30:51,583
But it could happen that you two end up alone together.

660
00:30:51,667 --> 00:30:53,333
What are you getting at?

661
00:30:53,917 --> 00:30:55,333
I don't like Balthazar.

662
00:30:55,417 --> 00:30:56,667
I like you.

663
00:30:58,917 --> 00:31:00,708
You're jealous, and you like the teacher?

664
00:31:01,542 --> 00:31:02,625
Well, he's not ugly.

665
00:31:02,875 --> 00:31:04,750
No, quite the opposite. He's very handsome.

666
00:31:05,625 --> 00:31:07,333
See? You do like him!

667
00:31:08,250 --> 00:31:09,542
I wouldn't mind.

668
00:31:09,625 --> 00:31:11,750
That's because you'd like that to happen.

669
00:31:11,833 --> 00:31:12,958
You're crazy!

670
00:31:13,458 --> 00:31:14,958
Look, you're being immature.

671
00:31:15,833 --> 00:31:18,208
And women mature faster than men.

672
00:31:19,333 --> 00:31:20,708
You're worrying me.

673
00:31:21,542 --> 00:31:22,750
What's worrying you?

674
00:31:24,792 --> 00:31:26,292
That I'm still a child.

675
00:31:28,375 --> 00:31:30,667
That I'm not mature enough to understand what I'm doing.

676
00:31:31,667 --> 00:31:33,083
[Martina] What are you doing?

677
00:31:33,208 --> 00:31:34,667
[Lucio] Taking your clothes off.

678
00:31:34,750 --> 00:31:36,542
♪ Music begins ♪

679
00:31:49,292 --> 00:31:50,583
♪ Music continues ♪

680
00:32:08,125 --> 00:32:09,292
♪ Music continues ♪

681
00:32:23,292 --> 00:32:24,292
♪ Music continues ♪

682
00:32:40,542 --> 00:32:41,542
Ten?

683
00:32:42,333 --> 00:32:43,833
♪ Music fades ♪

684
00:32:43,917 --> 00:32:44,917
I'm a virgin.

685
00:32:48,250 --> 00:32:49,625
I'm a virgin, and I'm Leal.

686
00:32:49,917 --> 00:32:50,917
♪ Music continues ♪

687
00:33:02,917 --> 00:33:04,292
♪ Music continues ♪

688
00:33:19,833 --> 00:33:21,125
♪ Music continues ♪

689
00:33:38,333 --> 00:33:39,625
♪ Music continues ♪

690
00:33:59,250 --> 00:34:00,750
♪ Music ends ♪

691
00:34:13,708 --> 00:34:16,250
- [Amelia] I want to be a photographer!
- [Lucio] What did you say?

692
00:34:16,917 --> 00:34:18,917
Since dancing isn't my thing...

693
00:34:19,667 --> 00:34:21,417
...I realized it, and I'm going to be a photographer.

694
00:34:21,750 --> 00:34:23,333
That's great! Like Tina Modotti.

695
00:34:24,083 --> 00:34:25,708
No, not like her, like

696
00:34:25,833 --> 00:34:27,417
the girl from Reaching for a Star.

697
00:34:27,875 --> 00:34:28,917
That's incredible!

698
00:34:29,250 --> 00:34:30,583
Female photographers are...

699
00:34:30,958 --> 00:34:32,375
They're very interesting.

700
00:34:32,458 --> 00:34:34,208
You found your passion so quickly!

701
00:34:34,417 --> 00:34:36,625
Yes, I realized that.

702
00:34:37,125 --> 00:34:38,208
Surprise!

703
00:34:39,625 --> 00:34:40,750
I love it!

704
00:34:40,917 --> 00:34:42,250
Amelia, a photographer?

705
00:34:42,750 --> 00:34:44,083
Congratulations!

706
00:34:44,917 --> 00:34:45,917
Thank you.

707
00:34:47,083 --> 00:34:48,583
Now I can take pictures of you two.

708
00:34:50,000 --> 00:34:51,042
As a couple...

709
00:34:52,792 --> 00:34:54,792
...dancing, naked.

710
00:34:54,875 --> 00:34:56,125
Isn't that amazing?

711
00:34:58,500 --> 00:34:59,750
It's amazing.

712
00:35:01,042 --> 00:35:02,125
[knocking at door]

713
00:35:02,208 --> 00:35:03,417
[Vicente] May I come in?

714
00:35:04,625 --> 00:35:05,958
My little brother!

715
00:35:07,292 --> 00:35:09,667
- [Lucio] How'd it go?
- [Vicente] How are you, you bastard?

716
00:35:09,750 --> 00:35:11,125
[Lucio] Good. And you? Look who's here!

717
00:35:11,208 --> 00:35:12,458
[Loles] Uncle!

718
00:35:12,542 --> 00:35:13,875
My love.

719
00:35:16,625 --> 00:35:18,500
And you, why weren't you answering the phone?

720
00:35:18,583 --> 00:35:20,667
Sorry, I had no signal, and...

721
00:35:21,125 --> 00:35:23,625
...when I got one, Lucio called and filled me in.

722
00:35:23,708 --> 00:35:25,417
You should've seen the look on his face when he saw me.

723
00:35:25,500 --> 00:35:27,292
I would've loved to be there.

724
00:35:27,375 --> 00:35:30,125
Well, I would've loved it if you'd told me sooner, man.

725
00:35:32,125 --> 00:35:33,125
- [Vicente] Yeah.
- [Loles] Yeah.

726
00:35:33,208 --> 00:35:34,750
- [Vicente] We have to talk.
- [Loles] We have to talk.

727
00:35:34,833 --> 00:35:36,708
No, there's nothing to talk about! Right now we have to celebrate

728
00:35:36,792 --> 00:35:38,125
and sort things out with Martina.

729
00:35:38,208 --> 00:35:39,292
He's told me everything.

730
00:35:39,375 --> 00:35:40,583
Are you serious about your plan?

731
00:35:40,667 --> 00:35:42,583
Man! I've never asked you for anything. Come on!

732
00:35:43,167 --> 00:35:46,083
Well, we'll always be indebted to you.

733
00:35:46,167 --> 00:35:47,167
- [Loles] Of course.
- [Vicente] Yes.

734
00:35:47,250 --> 00:35:49,167
Well, she can't suspect a thing, okay?

735
00:35:49,250 --> 00:35:51,667
[Loles] The truth is, I've wanted to be an
actress since I was little.

736
00:35:51,750 --> 00:35:53,500
But no one ever gave me a chance.

737
00:35:53,667 --> 00:35:55,458
And you're very good at pretending, darling.

738
00:35:55,542 --> 00:35:58,042
Besides, applause is right up my alley.

739
00:35:58,833 --> 00:36:00,958
[Lucio] Good, because we can't leave anything to chance.

740
00:36:01,042 --> 00:36:03,208
Dude, you haven't seen each other in twenty years.

741
00:36:03,292 --> 00:36:04,292
She knows nothing about you.

742
00:36:04,375 --> 00:36:05,875
- [Vicente] Calm down.
- [Lucio] She knows everything, man.

743
00:36:05,958 --> 00:36:08,167
We're soulmates. We've been connected since previous lives.

744
00:36:08,250 --> 00:36:09,500
- [Lucio] What would you know?
- [Loles] Hey, stop!

745
00:36:09,583 --> 00:36:10,958
Stop it. Those things scare me.

746
00:36:11,042 --> 00:36:13,417
Holy shit, you're intense, man!

747
00:36:13,500 --> 00:36:15,417
- [Lucio] Well, please!
- [Loles] All right, fine.

748
00:36:15,500 --> 00:36:16,792
But no kissing, okay?

749
00:36:16,875 --> 00:36:18,292
I don't want to confuse the baby.

750
00:36:18,375 --> 00:36:19,375
No kissing.

751
00:36:19,458 --> 00:36:22,042
Obviously, no kissing. Well, I'll leave you to get ready.

752
00:36:22,125 --> 00:36:23,125
Very well.

753
00:36:24,083 --> 00:36:25,083
Bye!

754
00:36:26,500 --> 00:36:28,458
So, have you told him yet?

755
00:36:28,542 --> 00:36:29,542
[Loles] Not at all!

756
00:36:29,833 --> 00:36:32,208
He's so nervous he hasn't even put two and two together.

757
00:36:32,292 --> 00:36:33,958
Either way, we have to tell him.

758
00:36:34,333 --> 00:36:36,125
Of course. That's why we came.

759
00:36:36,875 --> 00:36:38,708
But we have to wait for the right moment.

760
00:36:39,417 --> 00:36:40,625
It's his baby too.

761
00:36:41,750 --> 00:36:42,833
It's his sperm.

762
00:36:42,917 --> 00:36:44,292
- [Loles] The baby is ours.
- [Vicente] His sperm.

763
00:36:44,375 --> 00:36:46,792
- [Loles] Exactly!
- And he probably doesn't even remember.

764
00:36:47,958 --> 00:36:50,083
That woman has him completely distracted.

765
00:36:50,292 --> 00:36:52,958
Well, Martina is the love of his life.

766
00:36:53,208 --> 00:36:54,208
Come on!

767
00:36:55,083 --> 00:36:57,375
I think we have to wait until the very last moment of our lives

768
00:36:57,458 --> 00:36:58,625
to know who...

769
00:36:59,167 --> 00:37:01,458
...or who all the loves of our lives have been.

770
00:37:02,500 --> 00:37:04,583
I mean, if it weren't for that woman...

771
00:37:04,792 --> 00:37:06,125
...I'd think he was gay.

772
00:37:07,000 --> 00:37:09,042
What are you talking about, darling? Don't be ridiculous!

773
00:37:10,500 --> 00:37:13,875
Actually, when I first met you two, I thought
there was something between you...

774
00:37:13,958 --> 00:37:15,083
What?

775
00:37:15,167 --> 00:37:16,958
Loles, what are you talking about?

776
00:37:17,417 --> 00:37:19,125
[screams] You've completely ruined my nails!

777
00:37:19,208 --> 00:37:21,125
For fuck's sake!

778
00:37:21,208 --> 00:37:22,917
[car horn]

779
00:37:28,292 --> 00:37:29,583
[Beatriz] Bring your backpack and everything.

780
00:37:29,958 --> 00:37:31,958
[Beatriz] Oh, just look at you! Unbelievable!

781
00:37:33,250 --> 00:37:35,167
[Beatriz shouts] Martina!

782
00:37:35,708 --> 00:37:37,708
- [Martina] Coming!
- [Beatriz] Martina!

783
00:37:37,917 --> 00:37:39,542
[Beatriz shouts] We're here!

784
00:37:40,750 --> 00:37:43,083
[Beatriz gasps]
[Martina] Oh, how wonderful!

785
00:37:43,583 --> 00:37:46,125
I've wanted so badly to hug you, see you, touch you!

786
00:37:46,208 --> 00:37:48,792
- Look how thin you are! Beautiful!
- [Martina] Okay, enough. Tone it down.

787
00:37:48,875 --> 00:37:51,458
Queta! You've grown so much!

788
00:37:51,958 --> 00:37:53,458
Won't you give your aunt a kiss?

789
00:37:54,917 --> 00:37:56,417
[Martina] My beautiful girl.

790
00:37:56,792 --> 00:37:58,542
- [Enriqueta] You look beautiful, Auntie!
- [Martina] Mom.

791
00:37:58,708 --> 00:38:00,667
You can start calling me Mom. Just for today.

792
00:38:01,000 --> 00:38:03,083
Okay? Beatriz explained everything, right?

793
00:38:03,208 --> 00:38:05,292
- [Martina] Come in, come in.
- [Beatriz] Oh my goodness!

794
00:38:05,917 --> 00:38:07,292
- [Martina] Need a hand?
- [Enriqueta] Yes.

795
00:38:07,375 --> 00:38:08,708
What a huge house!

796
00:38:13,208 --> 00:38:14,792
[Beatriz] I never thought I'd be here.

797
00:38:14,875 --> 00:38:16,083
Don't cry.

798
00:38:16,417 --> 00:38:17,958
Don't start, Beatriz, okay?

799
00:38:18,042 --> 00:38:19,417
You've already been through enough with Enrique.

800
00:38:19,500 --> 00:38:21,167
- [Beatriz] Yes.
- [Enriqueta] Auntie...

801
00:38:21,333 --> 00:38:23,500
- [Enriqueta] Who's he?
- [Martina] Wait, Mom.

802
00:38:23,625 --> 00:38:25,958
- [Martina] Mom!
- Mom, who's he?

803
00:38:26,042 --> 00:38:27,042
He's my husband.

804
00:38:27,125 --> 00:38:29,833
But you told me my aunt was an old maid.

805
00:38:29,917 --> 00:38:31,667
Yes, sweetheart, yes. But he's a fake,

806
00:38:31,750 --> 00:38:33,125
just like you're his fake daughter.

807
00:38:33,208 --> 00:38:35,000
No! Don't listen to her.

808
00:38:35,083 --> 00:38:36,708
It's just so we can get used to it.

809
00:38:37,583 --> 00:38:38,833
Come here, Igor! Come.

810
00:38:39,542 --> 00:38:41,667
Hello. Nice to meet you. Igor.

811
00:38:42,917 --> 00:38:44,917
Beatriz. Nice to meet you.

812
00:38:45,375 --> 00:38:46,958
- [Beatriz] And this is Queta.
- [Martina] My daughter.

813
00:38:47,042 --> 00:38:49,708
Queta, my daughter. By the way, I have
something for you to wear tonight.

814
00:38:49,792 --> 00:38:50,792
Will you come with me?

815
00:38:50,917 --> 00:38:52,708
Oh, what are you going to give her?

816
00:38:52,792 --> 00:38:54,542
Take her to the kitchen, please.

817
00:38:55,042 --> 00:38:56,708
Don't spoil her!

818
00:38:56,792 --> 00:38:59,042
How are you related to Martina?

819
00:38:59,333 --> 00:39:00,375
Her sister.

820
00:39:00,917 --> 00:39:02,083
No! Wait, wait.

821
00:39:02,167 --> 00:39:04,125
I'm not really her husband, and the girl isn't her daughter.

822
00:39:04,208 --> 00:39:06,917
I'm her tenant. I rent a room from her.

823
00:39:07,000 --> 00:39:09,208
- [Igor] Who are you?
- [Beatriz] I'm her sister.

824
00:39:10,000 --> 00:39:11,208
[Beatriz] Same mother and father.

825
00:39:11,500 --> 00:39:13,667
Look, I may be drunk as hell, but I'm not going to mess this up.

826
00:39:13,750 --> 00:39:15,125
I mean, tell me who you are.

827
00:39:15,208 --> 00:39:16,250
Her sister!

828
00:39:16,917 --> 00:39:18,708
Fuck! You're intense!

829
00:39:21,000 --> 00:39:23,250
[Martina] Look, Queta, when I introduce you to him,

830
00:39:23,458 --> 00:39:26,500
show off the little necklace, discreetly.

831
00:39:26,583 --> 00:39:28,042
Lift your chin,

832
00:39:28,125 --> 00:39:29,708
and tug on the little horse.

833
00:39:29,792 --> 00:39:31,500
Naturally. Make it all look natural.

834
00:39:32,208 --> 00:39:34,667
And if he asks you something, tell him...

835
00:39:35,333 --> 00:39:36,833
"I found it in a drawer.

836
00:39:36,917 --> 00:39:39,792
And even though my mom hates it, I keep it."

837
00:39:40,458 --> 00:39:42,125
- [Enriqueta] Like this?
- [Martina] Perfect.

838
00:39:42,208 --> 00:39:43,875
You're so smart.

839
00:39:43,958 --> 00:39:46,458
I want to know why you and my mom don't talk.

840
00:39:46,542 --> 00:39:47,625
I am your mom, Queta!

841
00:39:47,708 --> 00:39:50,542
Then why don't you and my aunt talk?

842
00:39:52,500 --> 00:39:54,708
Look, if everything goes well at the theater tonight,

843
00:39:54,917 --> 00:39:56,333
I promise I'll tell you.

844
00:39:56,958 --> 00:39:57,958
Okay.

845
00:39:58,042 --> 00:39:59,250
Vicente, please!

846
00:39:59,667 --> 00:40:01,875
Come on, Lucio! Basically, what you're asking me

847
00:40:01,958 --> 00:40:03,667
is to go to the theater alone.

848
00:40:03,750 --> 00:40:05,792
- Just two hours, come on!
- [Vicente] Two... Darling!

849
00:40:06,208 --> 00:40:07,250
Where were you?

850
00:40:07,917 --> 00:40:09,375
Rehearsing in front of the mirror.

851
00:40:09,458 --> 00:40:10,792
An actor prepares.

852
00:40:11,083 --> 00:40:13,333
I went on YouTube to watch a Rossy de Palma tutorial,

853
00:40:13,417 --> 00:40:16,292
because being Vicente's wife isn't the same
as being Lucio's wife.

854
00:40:16,375 --> 00:40:17,625
[Lucio] What's the difference?

855
00:40:18,083 --> 00:40:19,500
Trade secrets.

856
00:40:19,625 --> 00:40:20,958
[they laugh]

857
00:40:21,250 --> 00:40:22,542
So, what were you talking about?

858
00:40:22,625 --> 00:40:24,542
[Lucio] Nothing. How to sort things out with the baby.

859
00:40:26,375 --> 00:40:27,833
You don't have to do anything, darling.
You've already done so much...

860
00:40:27,917 --> 00:40:29,375
- [Vicente] No! No.
- ...so just relax.

861
00:40:29,458 --> 00:40:30,583
I don't understand.

862
00:40:31,375 --> 00:40:32,750
[Vicente] Look, man,

863
00:40:33,375 --> 00:40:35,458
remember what we did when we were young?

864
00:40:36,083 --> 00:40:38,458
What we swore we'd never tell anyone?

865
00:40:38,542 --> 00:40:40,333
Dude, we were drunk. I don't even know why...!

866
00:40:40,417 --> 00:40:42,125
No, man! Not that!

867
00:40:42,208 --> 00:40:43,875
You two queers! I knew it.

868
00:40:43,958 --> 00:40:45,708
[Vicente] Give me a break, man!
[Loles screams]

869
00:40:46,083 --> 00:40:47,167
What happened?

870
00:40:47,333 --> 00:40:48,667
Okay, what's wrong, darling?

871
00:40:48,750 --> 00:40:49,792
Is it the baby?

872
00:40:49,875 --> 00:40:52,125
- [Vicente] What's wrong? I don't know.
- Who do I call? What do I do?

873
00:40:52,833 --> 00:40:55,000
I'm so good! I bet you believed me!

874
00:40:55,458 --> 00:40:56,625
Oh, for fuck's sake!

875
00:40:57,208 --> 00:40:59,042
I'm going to win a Goya, guys!

876
00:40:59,917 --> 00:41:01,292
[Lucio] You two are up to something.

877
00:41:01,708 --> 00:41:02,792
You don't understand a thing, but never mind.

878
00:41:02,875 --> 00:41:04,708
Well, now isn't the time.

879
00:41:04,958 --> 00:41:06,625
We're going to be late, aren't we?

880
00:41:06,708 --> 00:41:07,750
Let's go!

881
00:41:09,833 --> 00:41:12,250
[speaker] Who, if not society, has bound us to ideas

882
00:41:12,333 --> 00:41:14,750
that threaten our freedom?

883
00:41:16,917 --> 00:41:20,208
[speaker] Who told us love has only one form?

884
00:41:21,000 --> 00:41:23,000
That to belong to this society,

885
00:41:23,083 --> 00:41:25,667
we must restrict our own nature.

886
00:41:27,167 --> 00:41:29,417
What if we finally understand

887
00:41:29,500 --> 00:41:31,792
and listen to our bodies,

888
00:41:32,333 --> 00:41:33,625
our minds,

889
00:41:34,958 --> 00:41:36,208
and our hearts?

890
00:41:37,917 --> 00:41:39,083
[speaker] Who would we hurt?

891
00:41:39,167 --> 00:41:40,833
- [Lucio] No one!
- [Martina] No one!

892
00:41:44,750 --> 00:41:47,375
To take responsibility,

893
00:41:48,083 --> 00:41:50,333
to love and respect each other.

894
00:41:50,417 --> 00:41:52,958
That is why I invite you to discover my work.

895
00:41:53,208 --> 00:41:55,000
Let's sing to freedom!

896
00:41:55,167 --> 00:41:56,542
[applause]

897
00:42:02,708 --> 00:42:03,917
They're crazy.

898
00:42:04,000 --> 00:42:05,250
[Beatriz] They were only kisses.

899
00:42:05,333 --> 00:42:06,917
He won't be satisfied with just that.

900
00:42:08,208 --> 00:42:10,250
[Beatriz] I haven't seen any of what you're talking about.

901
00:42:10,333 --> 00:42:11,417
He suggested we have threesomes.

902
00:42:11,500 --> 00:42:13,958
[Amelia] If you'd been there, he'd probably
have suggested it to you too.

903
00:42:14,042 --> 00:42:16,417
- [Beatriz] All four of us?
- He insisted the three of us do things together!

904
00:42:16,500 --> 00:42:18,042
I don't understand why not all four.

905
00:42:18,125 --> 00:42:19,333
[Beatriz] Did you agree?

906
00:42:19,708 --> 00:42:20,917
I didn't.

907
00:42:21,000 --> 00:42:22,333
What about Martina?

908
00:42:27,750 --> 00:42:29,000
Martina's blinded by him.

909
00:42:29,542 --> 00:42:31,208
And I'm her only friend.

910
00:42:31,292 --> 00:42:33,167
I haven't had any choice but to start distancing myself from her.

911
00:42:33,250 --> 00:42:34,792
I don't know if you've noticed.

912
00:42:35,792 --> 00:42:37,667
Beatriz, I'm scared of losing her!

913
00:42:37,792 --> 00:42:39,208
But I can't do immoral things

914
00:42:39,292 --> 00:42:40,583
just to stay by her side.

915
00:42:41,125 --> 00:42:43,417
- We have to talk to her.
- [Amelia] No, no, no. Listen...

916
00:42:43,917 --> 00:42:45,625
Neither you nor I can do anything.

917
00:42:48,208 --> 00:42:49,750
[toilet flushes]

918
00:42:50,792 --> 00:42:52,708
Martina's a different person. He's changed her.

919
00:42:53,083 --> 00:42:55,250
If only your mother knew what I'm telling you...

920
00:42:55,333 --> 00:42:56,708
She'd kill him.

921
00:42:57,708 --> 00:42:59,000
She'd bring her closer to God!

922
00:43:00,208 --> 00:43:01,833
[on TV] Jorge Juan, wait!

923
00:43:02,750 --> 00:43:05,208
There's something very important you need to know.

924
00:43:08,167 --> 00:43:09,292
What do you want, Vilma?

925
00:43:11,000 --> 00:43:13,167
The baby I'm carrying

926
00:43:13,500 --> 00:43:14,500
isn't yours!

927
00:43:14,583 --> 00:43:15,583
♪ Suspenseful music ♪

928
00:43:15,750 --> 00:43:16,750
What?

929
00:43:17,375 --> 00:43:19,333
The baby I'm carrying

930
00:43:20,708 --> 00:43:22,458
doesn't belong to anyone!

931
00:43:26,250 --> 00:43:27,958
[on TV] I don't understand! Why did you do it?

932
00:43:30,125 --> 00:43:31,458
[on TV] Nobody must know.

933
00:43:32,000 --> 00:43:33,000
[Beatriz] Mom...

934
00:43:33,125 --> 00:43:34,417
[TV in background]

935
00:43:35,042 --> 00:43:36,083
Tell me.

936
00:43:36,750 --> 00:43:38,750
[Beatriz] Mom, can we talk?

937
00:43:41,500 --> 00:43:42,833
What's wrong?

938
00:43:43,958 --> 00:43:45,667
[Beatriz] Mom, there's something really serious

939
00:43:45,750 --> 00:43:47,083
I have to tell you.

940
00:43:49,125 --> 00:43:51,708
- [Mom] Are you pregnant?
- [Beatriz] No, Mom!

941
00:43:53,167 --> 00:43:54,167
But...

942
00:43:54,917 --> 00:43:56,875
...there are things you need to know.

943
00:43:58,042 --> 00:43:59,458
[TV in background]

944
00:44:12,875 --> 00:44:16,042
[Martina] Amelia, we waited for you all afternoon.

945
00:44:16,583 --> 00:44:18,708
Today we met Florentina Calle.

946
00:44:18,792 --> 00:44:20,625
She's a nude photographer.

947
00:44:21,125 --> 00:44:22,667
Her work is beautiful, Ame.

948
00:44:22,750 --> 00:44:24,083
She's the future.

949
00:44:24,542 --> 00:44:26,667
[Martina] Next weekend she's opening an exhibition

950
00:44:26,750 --> 00:44:28,417
in San Miguel de Allende.

951
00:44:28,875 --> 00:44:30,833
We have to be there, don't you think?

952
00:44:31,000 --> 00:44:33,250
Come on! Forget the argument.

953
00:44:33,625 --> 00:44:35,792
[Martina] Besides, tonight's party night.

954
00:44:35,875 --> 00:44:38,000
Love, Martina and Lucio.

955
00:44:38,208 --> 00:44:40,042
Oh, darling, my little cardigan. I'm cold.

956
00:44:40,125 --> 00:44:41,167
My cardigan.

957
00:44:41,375 --> 00:44:42,625
♪ Music begins ♪

958
00:44:52,667 --> 00:44:53,667
♪ Music continues ♪

959
00:45:00,417 --> 00:45:01,500
♪ Music ends ♪

960
00:45:01,583 --> 00:45:02,625
Did you meet her?

961
00:45:03,208 --> 00:45:04,292
[Lucio] Yes, I sure did.

962
00:45:04,708 --> 00:45:05,750
How well?

963
00:45:06,167 --> 00:45:07,333
Well enough.

964
00:45:09,042 --> 00:45:10,833
- [Lucio] I've spotted her. There she is.
- [Loles] Who?

965
00:45:11,208 --> 00:45:13,417
- [Loles] Where?
- Act natural, for fuck's sake!

966
00:45:13,500 --> 00:45:14,667
[Loles] But where?

967
00:45:15,208 --> 00:45:17,208
[Vicente whistles]
[Loles] Where? Where?

968
00:45:17,292 --> 00:45:18,917
I see her! I see her!

969
00:45:19,000 --> 00:45:20,500
I'm getting into character now.

970
00:45:23,000 --> 00:45:25,125
For now, take my hand.

971
00:45:25,667 --> 00:45:27,208
- [Lucio] Darling!
- [Loles] Yes, darling!

972
00:45:27,292 --> 00:45:29,250
What an incredible piece of art! Shall we go...?

973
00:45:29,333 --> 00:45:31,000
Of course, darling!

974
00:45:31,583 --> 00:45:32,583
[Loles] Let's see...

975
00:45:33,792 --> 00:45:35,708
I see him! I see him!

976
00:45:36,792 --> 00:45:37,875
Who are they?

977
00:45:37,958 --> 00:45:40,083
- [Igor] Must be the ones who are...
- [Martina] Act natural! Act natural!

978
00:45:40,167 --> 00:45:41,750
Act natural, act natural.

979
00:45:41,833 --> 00:45:43,042
She's pregnant.

980
00:45:43,125 --> 00:45:44,917
What do you mean she's pregnant? She's pregnant?

981
00:45:45,292 --> 00:45:46,542
- [Loles] No!
- [Igor] Very.

982
00:45:47,250 --> 00:45:48,375
No. You can't tell.

983
00:45:49,750 --> 00:45:50,792
[Igor] Yes. She is.

984
00:45:51,042 --> 00:45:52,292
You can't see her belly.

985
00:45:52,375 --> 00:45:53,375
There it is. Look!

986
00:45:54,875 --> 00:45:56,292
I can't believe it!

987
00:45:56,917 --> 00:45:58,750
He always said he didn't want children. I can't believe it.

988
00:45:58,833 --> 00:45:59,958
I just can't believe it!

989
00:46:00,042 --> 00:46:02,125
- [Igor] He said that?
- That the world was overpopulated,

990
00:46:02,208 --> 00:46:04,667
why bring children into it to suffer, blah, blah, blah.

991
00:46:04,750 --> 00:46:06,083
Well, he's right. I mean, I don't understand

992
00:46:06,167 --> 00:46:07,833
why people keep bringing kids into this world.

993
00:46:07,917 --> 00:46:10,042
- I mean, look how messed up it is!
- [Martina] Igor!

994
00:46:14,000 --> 00:46:15,250
With all due respect.

995
00:46:16,500 --> 00:46:17,583
[Martina] Hello!

996
00:46:17,958 --> 00:46:19,292
- [Martina] He saw me.
- [Lucio] She saw me.

997
00:46:19,375 --> 00:46:20,708
- [Loles] Already?
- [Lucio] Give me a kiss.

998
00:46:20,792 --> 00:46:22,333
- [Loles] Yes.
- [Vicente] Not on the lips.

999
00:46:24,500 --> 00:46:25,792
Normal! Igor, act normal.

1000
00:46:25,875 --> 00:46:27,500
Like normal people.

1001
00:46:27,583 --> 00:46:28,792
That's it, just like that.

1002
00:46:28,875 --> 00:46:30,125
Let's go, please, okay?

1003
00:46:31,458 --> 00:46:33,042
- [Martina] Let's go over there.
- [Igor] Where?

1004
00:46:33,458 --> 00:46:34,792
- [Loles] Give me your hand.
- [Lucio] Hold on to me, hold on.

1005
00:46:34,875 --> 00:46:36,208
Let me hold you instead.

1006
00:46:36,625 --> 00:46:38,250
- [Lucio] Fine, but I don't know.
- [Loles] Yes.

1007
00:46:38,500 --> 00:46:39,833
- [Martina] Hello!
- [Lucio] Hey!

1008
00:46:40,042 --> 00:46:41,333
- [Martina] How are you?
- [Loles] Hello.

1009
00:46:41,542 --> 00:46:43,583
Oh, no, the pleasure is mine, Marta!

1010
00:46:43,667 --> 00:46:44,917
- [Martina] Martina, Martina.
- [Lucio] Martina!

1011
00:46:45,000 --> 00:46:46,167
- [Martina] My husband...
- [Igor] Igor.

1012
00:46:46,250 --> 00:46:48,250
Nice to meet you. This is my wife, Loles.

1013
00:46:48,333 --> 00:46:50,708
[Martina] Delighted! And very pregnant, too. Beautiful.

1014
00:46:50,792 --> 00:46:52,500
- [Loles] You can tell, can't you?
- [Martina] You look gorgeous!

1015
00:46:52,583 --> 00:46:55,125
It's surprising because you always said you didn't want children.

1016
00:46:55,208 --> 00:46:56,833
So look, what a surprise!

1017
00:46:56,958 --> 00:46:58,458
[Lucio] Yes, surprise!

1018
00:46:58,833 --> 00:47:00,542
Life takes a lot of turns, doesn't it?

1019
00:47:00,625 --> 00:47:01,875
[Martina] Definitely.

1020
00:47:02,042 --> 00:47:04,333
Yes! Surprise, Lucio, you're going to be a father!

1021
00:47:05,000 --> 00:47:07,250
After many attempts and talks with the doctor,

1022
00:47:07,333 --> 00:47:08,667
calendars and tests...

1023
00:47:09,292 --> 00:47:10,458
...we did it.

1024
00:47:12,583 --> 00:47:15,375
He never imagined it himself, but he's going to be a dad.

1025
00:47:16,333 --> 00:47:18,125
I can't believe it. I'm going to be a dad.

1026
00:47:18,667 --> 00:47:21,625
He's taking a little time to process it, but he's getting there.

1027
00:47:21,708 --> 00:47:24,500
- [Lucio] It did catch me off guard.
- I can see that. The same happened to me.

1028
00:47:24,625 --> 00:47:26,042
It caught me by surprise.

1029
00:47:26,250 --> 00:47:28,542
I hardly noticed, and look how big the girl is now.

1030
00:47:28,625 --> 00:47:29,792
[Martina] Say hello, Queta.

1031
00:47:29,875 --> 00:47:30,875
Hello!

1032
00:47:30,958 --> 00:47:32,667
- [Loles] Queta?
- [Martina] Enriqueta.

1033
00:47:32,750 --> 00:47:34,792
Yes, like my father.

1034
00:47:35,292 --> 00:47:37,250
Igor! Enrique Igor.

1035
00:47:38,583 --> 00:47:40,250
Are you okay, Lucio?

1036
00:47:40,333 --> 00:47:43,417
Yes, I'm fine. I think I saw an old friend here.

1037
00:47:44,208 --> 00:47:46,417
That's a lot of reunions for one night, isn't it?

1038
00:47:46,625 --> 00:47:48,375
Where did you two meet?

1039
00:47:48,458 --> 00:47:50,375
In high school, about...

1040
00:47:50,458 --> 00:47:51,500
Twenty-five years ago.

1041
00:47:51,833 --> 00:47:53,417
[Lucio] We were best friends.

1042
00:47:54,333 --> 00:47:56,958
Us and Amelia. Oh, stop it, Igor, please.

1043
00:47:57,708 --> 00:47:59,417
- [Lucio] What's become of her?
- [Martina] Amelia?

1044
00:47:59,500 --> 00:48:00,708
- [Lucio] Yes.
- [Martina] She went into politics.

1045
00:48:00,792 --> 00:48:02,292
She wants to be a borough mayor.

1046
00:48:03,333 --> 00:48:04,583
But she was so stupid!

1047
00:48:04,667 --> 00:48:06,875
- [Martina] Exactly.
- Those people have no scruples.

1048
00:48:06,958 --> 00:48:09,417
- Who? Politicians or that girl?
- [Igor] Both.

1049
00:48:10,417 --> 00:48:13,083
She's running to head the Cuauhtémoc borough.

1050
00:48:13,417 --> 00:48:14,458
We'll see how it goes.

1051
00:48:14,792 --> 00:48:16,375
Remember what's there?

1052
00:48:17,458 --> 00:48:18,917
The last corner of the world.

1053
00:48:19,583 --> 00:48:21,250
What's the last corner of the world?

1054
00:48:22,083 --> 00:48:23,750
An old attic.

1055
00:48:24,583 --> 00:48:25,833
I see you two have a lot in common.

1056
00:48:25,917 --> 00:48:27,792
Yes, we know each other well.

1057
00:48:27,875 --> 00:48:30,833
That's why I'm surprised you got my name wrong.

1058
00:48:31,667 --> 00:48:33,208
And how many weeks along are you?

1059
00:48:33,292 --> 00:48:35,000
- [Loles] Thirty-eight.
- [Martina] That's great.

1060
00:48:35,375 --> 00:48:37,458
- [Lucio] Son of a... What a bastard!
- [Martina] What?

1061
00:48:37,708 --> 00:48:39,708
No, no. Time flies, doesn't it?

1062
00:48:39,833 --> 00:48:42,833
- [Lucio] It's crazy.
- This is all crazy, really.

1063
00:48:43,500 --> 00:48:46,750
You don't have to worry about anything,
darling. It's all settled.

1064
00:48:47,875 --> 00:48:49,333
[Loles] Does the little girl have a stiff neck?

1065
00:48:49,958 --> 00:48:51,167
Are you okay?

1066
00:48:51,292 --> 00:48:52,333
- [Enriqueta] Yes.
- [Loles] Yes?

1067
00:48:52,417 --> 00:48:53,792
[Lucio] I thought it was lost.

1068
00:48:54,000 --> 00:48:55,292
[Enriqueta] I found it in a drawer.

1069
00:48:55,375 --> 00:48:58,375
And even though my mom hates it, I keep it.

1070
00:48:59,167 --> 00:49:00,708
[Lucio] I gave that to your mommy.

1071
00:49:01,208 --> 00:49:02,417
Take good care of it, okay?

1072
00:49:03,125 --> 00:49:04,333
[Igor] The lights are dimming.

1073
00:49:04,417 --> 00:49:05,417
[Loles] Oh, that would be a shame.

1074
00:49:05,500 --> 00:49:08,583
- [Martina] No. That means it's...
- [Lucio] ...about to start.

1075
00:49:08,667 --> 00:49:09,792
[Loles] All right.

1076
00:49:09,875 --> 00:49:12,208
[Martina] A pleasure. Lovely meeting you.

1077
00:49:13,833 --> 00:49:15,333
[Loles] Did you like the surprise?

1078
00:49:15,750 --> 00:49:17,125
[Lucio] Vicente! Come here.

1079
00:49:17,208 --> 00:49:19,000
- [Loles] Lucio?
- I need to talk to this asshole.

1080
00:49:19,083 --> 00:49:21,042
Vicente! Vicente, come here, man!

1081
00:49:21,292 --> 00:49:22,708
Get over here, you bastard!

1082
00:49:23,125 --> 00:49:25,208
- [Lucio] Excuse me.
- [Loles] Sorry, sorry. Lucio!

1083
00:49:26,167 --> 00:49:27,250
[Amelia] Martina!

1084
00:49:28,083 --> 00:49:29,208
[Loles] Guys!

1085
00:49:29,750 --> 00:49:30,833
[Amelia] Martina!

1086
00:49:31,667 --> 00:49:32,917
Where were you?

1087
00:49:34,417 --> 00:49:37,000
- [Lucio] We thought you weren't coming.
- [Amelia] You wish.

1088
00:49:37,125 --> 00:49:38,667
- [Martina] Did you see our gift?
- [Amelia] I loved it.

1089
00:49:38,750 --> 00:49:40,417
So, what did you think about San Miguel?

1090
00:49:41,167 --> 00:49:43,417
It's three hours away! She's going to be there.

1091
00:49:43,500 --> 00:49:44,792
[Amelia] And so are we.

1092
00:49:45,667 --> 00:49:47,125
Lucio? Did you hear that?

1093
00:49:47,208 --> 00:49:48,625
The San Miguel plan is on.

1094
00:49:48,708 --> 00:49:49,708
[Lucio] Awesome!

1095
00:49:50,042 --> 00:49:51,500
I have to think of something to tell my mother.

1096
00:49:51,583 --> 00:49:53,125
The teacher isn't coming, right?

1097
00:49:53,958 --> 00:49:55,167
No. He's not going.

1098
00:49:55,417 --> 00:49:56,917
Then I can try out my new driver's license.

1099
00:49:57,000 --> 00:49:58,667
[Martina] Are you seriously saying what I think you're saying?

1100
00:49:58,750 --> 00:50:00,333
What do you think I drove here?

1101
00:50:00,417 --> 00:50:01,625
[Martina screams]

1102
00:50:03,625 --> 00:50:05,250
[Lucio] Have you heard what they're going to play?

1103
00:50:06,208 --> 00:50:07,458
[Martina] Let's go to the front!

1104
00:50:07,667 --> 00:50:09,083
[Balthazar] Anyone want chocolates?

1105
00:50:10,208 --> 00:50:11,250
[Martina] What kind?

1106
00:50:11,667 --> 00:50:12,667
Mushrooms!

1107
00:50:12,833 --> 00:50:14,333
♪ Music begins ♪

1108
00:50:18,583 --> 00:50:20,625
♪ I could begin ♪

1109
00:50:22,583 --> 00:50:24,292
♪ By saying that ♪

1110
00:50:25,125 --> 00:50:28,333
♪ Neither of us ♪

1111
00:50:28,417 --> 00:50:30,750
♪ Is to blame... ♪

1112
00:50:33,708 --> 00:50:35,458
[Lucio] We had a deal.

1113
00:50:36,333 --> 00:50:38,208
I could never remember if I had to tell you

1114
00:50:38,292 --> 00:50:39,875
before or after using them.

1115
00:50:40,208 --> 00:50:42,250
Dude, you're talking like they were a pair of shoes.

1116
00:50:42,333 --> 00:50:43,708
I gave you sperm, for fuck's sake!

1117
00:50:43,792 --> 00:50:45,292
You didn't just give us your sperm.

1118
00:50:45,375 --> 00:50:47,333
You gave us the chance to become

1119
00:50:47,500 --> 00:50:49,958
the happiest couple on the face of the earth.

1120
00:50:50,042 --> 00:50:52,333
Yeah, man, but you could have told me sooner, right?

1121
00:50:52,417 --> 00:50:55,167
Dude, we flew all the way from Madrid to tell you.

1122
00:50:55,458 --> 00:50:58,292
But this whole situation with Martina has
turned you into an idiot.

1123
00:50:58,375 --> 00:51:00,083
- [Lucio] Now I don't know what to do.
- [Vicente] No!

1124
00:51:00,167 --> 00:51:03,042
You don't have to do anything. Seriously, nothing.

1125
00:51:03,125 --> 00:51:04,708
We're going to be great parents.

1126
00:51:05,000 --> 00:51:06,667
Just like I promised you outside the clinic,

1127
00:51:06,750 --> 00:51:08,375
the day they gave me the news.

1128
00:51:09,000 --> 00:51:10,500
[Lucio] That was so long ago.

1129
00:51:10,583 --> 00:51:12,583
[Vicente] You're my best friend. You always have been.

1130
00:51:12,667 --> 00:51:15,667
I hope all this hasn't changed your mind.

1131
00:51:16,083 --> 00:51:17,667
Of course not, man. Come on!

1132
00:51:18,292 --> 00:51:21,708
Good, you bastard, because it's too late to back out anyway.

1133
00:51:22,833 --> 00:51:24,125
You fucking idiot!

1134
00:51:24,458 --> 00:51:26,417
Lucio, for my part, all I can say

1135
00:51:26,875 --> 00:51:29,125
is that what you did was an act of love.

1136
00:51:29,208 --> 00:51:30,417
[woman shushes]

1137
00:51:31,167 --> 00:51:33,542
Well, it was just to improve the gene pool.

1138
00:51:33,792 --> 00:51:35,417
- [Vicente] Don't be a jerk.
- [woman] Enough.

1139
00:51:35,500 --> 00:51:38,333
♪ Walking arm in arm ♪

1140
00:51:38,417 --> 00:51:43,458
♪ Escaping together to nowhere ♪

1141
00:51:48,167 --> 00:51:51,750
♪ We find each other again ♪

1142
00:51:52,125 --> 00:51:55,875
♪ After so many years ♪

1143
00:51:55,958 --> 00:51:59,833
♪ Just one more time ♪

1144
00:52:00,083 --> 00:52:01,750
[audience cheering]

1145
00:52:03,875 --> 00:52:07,583
♪ Holding hands ♪

1146
00:52:07,792 --> 00:52:11,500
♪ With the world under our arms ♪

1147
00:52:11,917 --> 00:52:15,833
♪ Without looking back... ♪

1148
00:52:26,333 --> 00:52:28,333
It's time to close that chapter, Lucio.

1149
00:52:29,875 --> 00:52:30,875
Something doesn't add up.

1150
00:52:30,958 --> 00:52:32,208
Just let her go!

1151
00:52:36,583 --> 00:52:39,083
Loles, can I ask you a favor?

1152
00:52:39,500 --> 00:52:40,542
I knew this was coming.

1153
00:52:41,500 --> 00:52:43,667
When we leave, can you invite them to dinner?

1154
00:52:45,208 --> 00:52:47,083
- [Loles] Are you crazy?
- [Vicente] What's going on?

1155
00:52:47,375 --> 00:52:49,792
He wants us all to go out to dinner afterward!

1156
00:52:49,875 --> 00:52:51,875
No, no. We have to put an end to this charade.

1157
00:52:51,958 --> 00:52:54,000
All this acting is exhausting. No!

1158
00:52:54,083 --> 00:52:55,625
And what am I supposed to do?

1159
00:52:55,708 --> 00:52:57,125
- [Lucio] Wait!
- [Vicente] What?

1160
00:52:57,208 --> 00:52:59,667
For not telling me about the pregnancy, man.
You'll wait, damn it!

1161
00:53:00,458 --> 00:53:02,083
[in English] Don't be so uncouth.

1162
00:53:02,167 --> 00:53:03,542
Be quiet so I can watch.

1163
00:53:03,625 --> 00:53:05,667
You haven't stopped talking all night.

1164
00:53:05,750 --> 00:53:07,042
[in English] She's right, she's right.

1165
00:53:07,125 --> 00:53:08,750
But don't speak to me that way,

1166
00:53:08,833 --> 00:53:11,000
because I'm a pregnant woman, okay?

1167
00:53:16,875 --> 00:53:18,042
[applause]

1168
00:53:18,125 --> 00:53:20,125
♪ Music ends ♪

1169
00:53:25,333 --> 00:53:26,792
Go find your sister.

1170
00:53:26,917 --> 00:53:28,917
But Mom, she's going to get really angry.

1171
00:53:29,000 --> 00:53:32,333
You don't want to make Him angry, Beatriz!

1172
00:53:34,375 --> 00:53:35,750
[shouting in background]

1173
00:53:36,417 --> 00:53:37,750
Hey, teacher!

1174
00:53:39,708 --> 00:53:40,875
[Balthazar] Who are you?

1175
00:53:41,000 --> 00:53:42,875
I'm Bea, Martina's sister.

1176
00:53:42,958 --> 00:53:44,333
I really need to find her.

1177
00:53:44,417 --> 00:53:45,583
Want some?

1178
00:53:45,667 --> 00:53:47,208
[Beatriz] I'm starving!

1179
00:54:01,708 --> 00:54:04,542
[Beatriz] Martina! Martina!

1180
00:54:05,292 --> 00:54:06,750
Bea! What are you doing here?

1181
00:54:07,208 --> 00:54:08,542
[Beatriz] It's Mom!

1182
00:54:08,833 --> 00:54:10,417
- [Martina] What?
- [Beatriz] It's Mom!

1183
00:54:10,500 --> 00:54:11,583
[Martina] What happened to Mom?

1184
00:54:11,667 --> 00:54:14,333
[Beatriz] We have to go. She's waiting outside.

1185
00:54:14,667 --> 00:54:15,875
[Lucio] What happened?

1186
00:54:15,958 --> 00:54:17,833
[Beatriz] Mom is furious.

1187
00:54:18,417 --> 00:54:20,167
No, hey, hey. Don't make things worse.

1188
00:54:20,250 --> 00:54:22,500
You haven't had any good ideas lately.

1189
00:54:22,583 --> 00:54:23,917
[Balthazar] What's going on?

1190
00:54:24,083 --> 00:54:27,167
What's going on is you're high as a kite, dear teacher.

1191
00:54:33,042 --> 00:54:35,500
- [Mom] You'll never see this... again.
- [Lucio] Martina!

1192
00:54:35,583 --> 00:54:37,792
- [Mom] Martina!
- [Lucio] Martina!

1193
00:54:40,333 --> 00:54:41,667
♪ Xylophone notes ♪

1194
00:54:49,458 --> 00:54:50,458
[gust of wind]

1195
00:54:52,000 --> 00:54:53,000
Wow!

1196
00:54:53,125 --> 00:54:54,417
♪ Xylophone notes ♪

1197
00:54:54,500 --> 00:54:56,667
[Lucio] Isn't it true, angel of love!

1198
00:54:57,125 --> 00:54:59,292
- [Beatriz] Romeo!
- [Lucio] That on this secluded shore...

1199
00:54:59,375 --> 00:55:02,125
- [Beatriz] Romeo!
- [Lucio] Bea, I'm not Romeo. I'm Lucio.

1200
00:55:02,583 --> 00:55:05,000
[Beatriz] You're an angel who's flown to my balcony.

1201
00:55:05,083 --> 00:55:07,417
Where's Martina? Open the door!
[knocking at door]

1202
00:55:11,458 --> 00:55:13,583
Where's Martina? What did you tell your mother?

1203
00:55:13,667 --> 00:55:16,958
You're the most beautiful man my eyes have ever seen.

1204
00:55:17,083 --> 00:55:19,000
What are you up to? What did you tell your mother?

1205
00:55:19,083 --> 00:55:20,083
Where's Martina?

1206
00:55:20,167 --> 00:55:22,042
Why do you prefer her to me?

1207
00:55:22,292 --> 00:55:24,000
I've always wanted you,

1208
00:55:24,083 --> 00:55:25,833
I've always wanted to kiss your li...

1209
00:55:25,917 --> 00:55:27,417
What's wrong with you?

1210
00:55:29,625 --> 00:55:30,917
[Lucio] What did you eat?

1211
00:55:32,708 --> 00:55:33,875
[Lucio] Did Baltha give you something?

1212
00:55:36,250 --> 00:55:38,625
- [Lucio] Are you on drugs?
- [Beatriz] It's a sin...

1213
00:55:40,250 --> 00:55:41,375
[gasps]

1214
00:55:41,458 --> 00:55:43,167
What are you doing here?

1215
00:55:43,250 --> 00:55:45,208
[Lucio] I just wanted to see if you were okay.

1216
00:55:45,292 --> 00:55:47,917
Oh! That gossip told her everything. You're so jealous.

1217
00:55:48,042 --> 00:55:50,292
- You always want what I have!
- [Beatriz] Shut up!

1218
00:55:50,375 --> 00:55:51,542
[Mom] Everything okay?

1219
00:55:51,625 --> 00:55:53,375
Leave her alone. She's high. She ate mushrooms.

1220
00:55:55,167 --> 00:55:56,917
- [Mom] Girls?
- Go before they catch you.

1221
00:55:57,000 --> 00:55:58,292
[Lucio] Just tell me everything's okay.

1222
00:55:58,375 --> 00:56:00,417
They know about the last corner of the world!

1223
00:56:00,500 --> 00:56:02,083
And God knows what else Bea told her.

1224
00:56:02,167 --> 00:56:03,750
[Martina] She's going to talk to the school principal.

1225
00:56:03,833 --> 00:56:06,042
- [Lucio] To have me expelled?
- [Martina] No, to separate us.

1226
00:56:06,125 --> 00:56:07,833
- [Mom] Martina!
- [Lucio] Then let's tell them the truth.

1227
00:56:07,917 --> 00:56:10,083
No, they don't know about Baltha. Better leave it at that.

1228
00:56:10,167 --> 00:56:12,958
- [Lucio] And San Miguel?
- [Martina] I don't know. Not now.

1229
00:56:13,042 --> 00:56:15,042
[Mom shouts] Martina!

1230
00:56:15,125 --> 00:56:16,542
[Lucio] We have to go!

1231
00:56:16,667 --> 00:56:18,333
♪ Music begins ♪

1232
00:56:19,958 --> 00:56:21,125
What happened?

1233
00:56:21,208 --> 00:56:22,875
- [Martina] Mom...
- [Mom] What?

1234
00:56:22,958 --> 00:56:24,458
We have to talk about Bea.

1235
00:56:25,375 --> 00:56:27,542
Oh, Beatriz!

1236
00:56:27,625 --> 00:56:29,125
♪ Music continues ♪

1237
00:56:29,208 --> 00:56:34,042
♪ When I look through the glass ♪

1238
00:56:36,208 --> 00:56:40,167
♪ I look through time... ♪

1239
00:56:40,250 --> 00:56:42,583
[teacher] Six, six, nine, six, six, four.

1240
00:56:43,875 --> 00:56:46,333
Ninety-five, fifty-five, twenty-nine.

1241
00:56:47,917 --> 00:56:50,542
Ninety-five, fifty-five, twenty-nine!

1242
00:56:50,625 --> 00:56:51,958
They moved him to another classroom.

1243
00:56:52,042 --> 00:56:54,958
♪ Where fears evaporate... ♪

1244
00:56:55,083 --> 00:56:57,458
[teacher] Ninety-nine, sixty-four, forty.

1245
00:56:57,542 --> 00:57:03,042
♪ And I take the chance to unfold myself ♪

1246
00:57:04,708 --> 00:57:06,042
♪ To get out of the glass... ♪

1247
00:57:06,125 --> 00:57:09,083
- [Martina] I won't be able to go anymore.
- You have to make an effort.

1248
00:57:09,542 --> 00:57:11,750
[Martina] We could get in trouble.

1249
00:57:11,833 --> 00:57:14,833
[Balthazar] It's a risk the three of us have to take.

1250
00:57:19,208 --> 00:57:23,750
♪ I search for your face in my memory ♪

1251
00:57:26,250 --> 00:57:30,917
♪ And I don't know why... ♪

1252
00:57:31,000 --> 00:57:33,875
If I see him talking to that young lady, I'll expel him.

1253
00:57:33,958 --> 00:57:38,542
♪ I don't care to know why ♪

1254
00:57:39,083 --> 00:57:42,125
♪ Don't let ♪

1255
00:57:42,208 --> 00:57:45,792
♪ The devil devour us, my love ♪

1256
00:57:45,875 --> 00:57:49,167
♪ Let him swallow your warmth ♪

1257
00:57:49,250 --> 00:57:52,667
♪ Let him belch out my pain ♪

1258
00:57:53,250 --> 00:57:56,042
♪ Don't let ♪

1259
00:57:56,458 --> 00:57:59,792
♪ The devil devour us, my love... ♪

1260
00:58:00,667 --> 00:58:02,917
You have to do something, or I'll tell Martina

1261
00:58:03,000 --> 00:58:05,000
who put that idea in my head.

1262
00:58:05,083 --> 00:58:07,625
[Beatriz] We're doing the right thing. Don't
be stupid and ruin everything.

1263
00:58:07,708 --> 00:58:10,625
I may be stupid, but don't try to outsmart me.

1264
00:58:10,708 --> 00:58:11,750
Help her!

1265
00:58:13,458 --> 00:58:14,833
Idiot!

1266
00:58:16,375 --> 00:58:21,417
♪ I fly away and you are my guide... ♪

1267
00:58:21,667 --> 00:58:23,125
Here's the brochure.

1268
00:58:23,625 --> 00:58:25,167
It's from Friday to Sunday.

1269
00:58:26,500 --> 00:58:29,500
[Amelia] And it's a retreat to find ourselves.

1270
00:58:29,917 --> 00:58:31,125
And God.

1271
00:58:33,750 --> 00:58:35,417
Don't worry. I talked to Miss Ximena.

1272
00:58:35,500 --> 00:58:36,875
She's going to cover for us.

1273
00:58:37,083 --> 00:58:38,625
She turned out to be nicer than the teacher on Carrusel!

1274
00:58:38,708 --> 00:58:40,500
- [Beatriz] I swear.
- [Martina] Okay...

1275
00:58:41,125 --> 00:58:43,125
- [Mom] Please!
- [Amelia] Hello.

1276
00:58:43,458 --> 00:58:45,708
- [Mom] Hello, how are you?
- [Amelia] How are you, ma'am?

1277
00:58:45,917 --> 00:58:48,333
[Mom] Thanks for finding another spot for my Beatriz.

1278
00:58:48,417 --> 00:58:50,417
[Amelia] Don't worry. My aunt should be here any minute.

1279
00:58:50,500 --> 00:58:52,083
[car horn]
[Amelia] Auntie! Auntie!

1280
00:58:52,167 --> 00:58:54,500
- [Amelia] Come on, let's go.
- [Mom] Goodbye.

1281
00:58:55,000 --> 00:58:56,500
[Mom] Take care. Bye.

1282
00:58:57,958 --> 00:58:59,583
I hope I don't get fired.

1283
00:59:02,167 --> 00:59:03,542
Girls, hurry up.

1284
00:59:03,625 --> 00:59:04,792
Thank you.

1285
00:59:05,083 --> 00:59:07,875
♪ Don't let ♪

1286
00:59:07,958 --> 00:59:11,500
♪ The devil devour us, my love ♪

1287
00:59:11,583 --> 00:59:15,083
♪ Let him swallow your warmth ♪

1288
00:59:15,167 --> 00:59:17,250
♪ Let him belch out my pain ♪

1289
00:59:17,333 --> 00:59:18,583
[applause]

1290
00:59:21,583 --> 00:59:22,917
♪ Music ends ♪

1291
00:59:27,958 --> 00:59:30,792
[Martina] Please, Igor, behave. That's enough.

1292
00:59:31,167 --> 00:59:33,333
- [Lucio] Fate.
- [Martina] Oh, I see, yes.

1293
00:59:33,417 --> 00:59:34,708
[Loles] And the girl?

1294
00:59:34,792 --> 00:59:36,583
- [Martina] Oh God, the girl!
- [Igor] Roberta is very restless.

1295
00:59:36,667 --> 00:59:38,750
Queta, Queta. Queta!

1296
00:59:39,000 --> 00:59:40,083
Queta!

1297
00:59:41,375 --> 00:59:43,917
- [Martina] Queta!
- [Enriqueta] I couldn't find you.

1298
00:59:44,417 --> 00:59:46,750
[Martina] Oh, child! Where have you been?

1299
00:59:46,833 --> 00:59:48,958
[Igor] You need to keep an eye on your daughter, Martina.

1300
00:59:49,042 --> 00:59:51,208
Yes, darling, yes. Please don't wander off.

1301
00:59:52,333 --> 00:59:53,708
Wow, I'm starving!

1302
00:59:53,792 --> 00:59:55,417
By the way, where are you having dinner?

1303
00:59:55,500 --> 00:59:56,958
[Martina] At home, because of the little girl.

1304
00:59:57,042 --> 00:59:59,208
- [Igor] We could have dinner together.
- [Loles] Oh, yes!

1305
00:59:59,375 --> 01:00:01,583
Uh, I'm sure they want to see San Miguel,

1306
01:00:01,667 --> 01:00:03,375
and we're heading home because of the girl.

1307
01:00:03,458 --> 01:00:04,750
[Igor] Well, have them over for dinner.

1308
01:00:04,833 --> 01:00:06,375
I haven't prepared anything, Igor.

1309
01:00:06,458 --> 01:00:08,292
[Igor] But we have the new cook.

1310
01:00:08,375 --> 01:00:10,208
- [Igor] The little one with the big nose.
- [Lucio] Sounds good.

1311
01:00:10,292 --> 01:00:12,083
We can improvise something, right?

1312
01:00:12,167 --> 01:00:14,083
Well, if that's what you want.

1313
01:00:14,167 --> 01:00:15,708
I love improvising.

1314
01:00:15,792 --> 01:00:17,917
Lucio! Lucio!

1315
01:00:18,000 --> 01:00:19,583
Well, let's go, shall we? Come on, let's go.

1316
01:00:19,667 --> 01:00:20,833
- [Vicente] Lucio!
- [Martina] A gentleman is calling you.

1317
01:00:20,917 --> 01:00:22,292
[Lucio] For fuck's sake.

1318
01:00:22,375 --> 01:00:23,500
[Vicente] Where are you going?

1319
01:00:23,583 --> 01:00:25,208
[Lucio] This is the friend I told you about.

1320
01:00:25,292 --> 01:00:27,250
- [Martina] Oh, lovely! I'm Martina.
- [Vicente] Vicente, nice to meet you.

1321
01:00:27,333 --> 01:00:28,542
Hello, Igor!

1322
01:00:28,625 --> 01:00:29,750
My husband, my daughter Queta...

1323
01:00:29,833 --> 01:00:31,417
And how do you two know each other?

1324
01:00:31,500 --> 01:00:33,792
From... Oh, we're childhood friends, yes.

1325
01:00:33,875 --> 01:00:35,583
[Vicente] Great play, wasn't it? Did you like it?

1326
01:00:35,667 --> 01:00:38,583
Yes, it was great. But we're leaving. I'll
call you from the hotel later.

1327
01:00:38,667 --> 01:00:40,417
[Igor] Hey, but you really wanted to see him, right?

1328
01:00:40,500 --> 01:00:42,750
- [Igor] Invite him to dinner at our house.
- [Loles] Of course!

1329
01:00:42,833 --> 01:00:44,958
I'll go ahead and give the cook a quick call.

1330
01:00:45,042 --> 01:00:46,292
Sure, sure, sure.

1331
01:00:46,375 --> 01:00:48,125
[Igor] Come on, sweetheart, give me your hand.

1332
01:00:48,583 --> 01:00:49,750
[Lucio gets Loles's attention]

1333
01:00:49,833 --> 01:00:51,958
- [Loles] Oh, sorry.
- [Lucio] You're a bastard.

1334
01:00:53,333 --> 01:00:55,333
♪ Music begins ♪

1335
01:00:58,125 --> 01:01:00,208
- [Lucio] Not that one.
- [Amelia] It's great!

1336
01:01:00,292 --> 01:01:02,417
- [Amelia] Turn it up, turn it up.
- [Lucio] Amelia, no!

1337
01:01:02,500 --> 01:01:04,708
♪ The tears of a deception ♪

1338
01:01:04,875 --> 01:01:08,625
♪ At the worst possible time came that barroom pirate ♪

1339
01:01:08,708 --> 01:01:12,667
♪ Who offered me an island at the bottom of the sea ♪

1340
01:01:12,917 --> 01:01:16,250
♪ And one night he took me ♪

1341
01:01:16,333 --> 01:01:19,750
♪ On a honeymoon without crossing the threshold ♪

1342
01:01:20,250 --> 01:01:23,708
♪ In your sigh and an engine ♪

1343
01:01:24,750 --> 01:01:27,208
♪ A grave destiny ♪

1344
01:01:27,292 --> 01:01:29,167
♪ Yellow and blue ♪

1345
01:01:29,250 --> 01:01:30,875
♪ In the half-light ♪

1346
01:01:30,958 --> 01:01:34,833
♪ I paint your kisses in colors ♪

1347
01:01:34,917 --> 01:01:36,833
♪ Yellow, blue... ♪

1348
01:01:39,125 --> 01:01:41,500
[Igor] So glad you came. Welcome!

1349
01:01:41,583 --> 01:01:43,500
Let them in.
[Enriqueta complains]

1350
01:01:43,583 --> 01:01:45,792
[Igor] Let them go first. Welcome.

1351
01:01:46,708 --> 01:01:49,083
[Martina] Please, come in. Welcome.

1352
01:01:49,167 --> 01:01:51,083
- [Igor] Welcome, come in.
- [Loles] Excuse me.

1353
01:01:51,167 --> 01:01:53,208
- [Lucio] Thank you.
- [Loles] Oh, what a beautiful house.

1354
01:01:53,292 --> 01:01:54,833
It's such a pleasure. Please, come in.

1355
01:01:54,917 --> 01:01:56,958
- [Loles] It's gorgeous, really.
- [Lucio] Wow, so elegant!

1356
01:01:57,042 --> 01:01:58,833
Goodness, and you said you hadn't prepared anything.

1357
01:01:58,917 --> 01:02:01,417
[Igor] Our new cook is a gem, man.

1358
01:02:01,500 --> 01:02:03,750
- [Loles] It's almost too pretty to sit down.
- [Martina] Oh, no! Please.

1359
01:02:03,833 --> 01:02:05,000
Have a seat. Make yourselves at home.

1360
01:02:05,083 --> 01:02:07,125
I'm going to the kitchen to see if dinner is ready.

1361
01:02:07,208 --> 01:02:08,542
[Loles] Oh, how delicious! Wonderful!

1362
01:02:08,625 --> 01:02:10,583
- [Enriqueta] I'm not hungry.
- [Igor] Go to your seat.

1363
01:02:10,667 --> 01:02:13,250
- [Enriqueta] Where's my seat?
- [Lucio] Chente!

1364
01:02:13,333 --> 01:02:15,375
- [Igor] That's my seat.
- [Vicente] Oh...

1365
01:02:15,583 --> 01:02:17,000
What's wrong with you?

1366
01:02:17,292 --> 01:02:19,083
[Beatriz] Oh! I wanted to surprise you.

1367
01:02:19,167 --> 01:02:20,458
- [Beatriz] Didn't you like it?
- [Martina] No.

1368
01:02:20,542 --> 01:02:23,417
The idea is for you to leave quickly, not move in here.

1369
01:02:23,500 --> 01:02:25,458
But I'd already set the table.

1370
01:02:26,042 --> 01:02:27,667
We haven't had dinner together in so long...

1371
01:02:27,750 --> 01:02:30,208
Don't even think about coming out, you hear me?

1372
01:02:30,333 --> 01:02:32,208
- [Loles] Excuse me...
- [Martina] Oh! Loles.

1373
01:02:32,292 --> 01:02:34,750
- I'm looking for the cook.
- [Martina] Oh, here she is.

1374
01:02:34,833 --> 01:02:36,250
- [Loles] Hello, nice to meet you.
- [Beatriz] Hello.

1375
01:02:36,333 --> 01:02:37,875
You see, I have a little question.

1376
01:02:37,958 --> 01:02:39,125
Since I'm pregnant,

1377
01:02:39,208 --> 01:02:40,958
I'd like to know if there's anything I shouldn't eat.

1378
01:02:41,042 --> 01:02:43,542
[Martina] Uh, no! You can eat everything here.

1379
01:02:43,625 --> 01:02:45,125
- [Loles] Oh, wonderful!
- [Martina] Of course.

1380
01:02:45,208 --> 01:02:48,458
- [Loles] Everything smells delicious.
- [Martina] Come on, let's get started.

1381
01:02:48,542 --> 01:02:50,208
Well, it's truly lovely to meet you.

1382
01:02:52,125 --> 01:02:54,292
[calling] Spanish lady, come here!

1383
01:02:54,958 --> 01:02:57,792
[Beatriz] Hey, did you see the chocolates in
the middle of the table?

1384
01:02:58,417 --> 01:03:00,500
- [Loles] Oh, yes.
- [Beatriz] Don't touch them.

1385
01:03:01,083 --> 01:03:02,417
Okay, okay.

1386
01:03:03,958 --> 01:03:05,333
Why? What's in them?

1387
01:03:05,417 --> 01:03:07,250
An old recipe from my dance teacher.

1388
01:03:08,583 --> 01:03:09,875
[Beatriz] Come on, bye.

1389
01:03:10,250 --> 01:03:12,000
Well, how mysterious!

1390
01:03:14,250 --> 01:03:15,583
[car horn]

1391
01:03:15,667 --> 01:03:16,917
[dog barking]

1392
01:03:21,667 --> 01:03:23,000
[engine running]

1393
01:03:33,042 --> 01:03:34,417
Okay, we're here.

1394
01:03:35,083 --> 01:03:36,250
[Martina] Already?

1395
01:03:36,333 --> 01:03:37,667
[Beatriz] Oh, thank goodness!

1396
01:03:38,292 --> 01:03:40,417
[Lucio] Amelia, get out of the car.
[Beatriz complains]

1397
01:03:40,500 --> 01:03:42,458
Nothing's going to happen to them. It's just spray.

1398
01:03:42,542 --> 01:03:44,208
♪ Music begins ♪

1399
01:03:48,417 --> 01:03:50,125
[Lucio] Seahorses...

1400
01:03:50,333 --> 01:03:51,875
[Amelia] Didn't you say she photographed nudes?

1401
01:03:51,958 --> 01:03:53,583
[Lucio] That's what my dad said.

1402
01:03:54,958 --> 01:03:56,958
[Lucio] "They can't live without each other,

1403
01:03:57,625 --> 01:03:59,875
which is why they say seahorses

1404
01:03:59,958 --> 01:04:01,250
die of love."

1405
01:04:02,458 --> 01:04:03,875
I have to meet her!

1406
01:04:04,583 --> 01:04:06,042
I need to use the bathroom.

1407
01:04:08,000 --> 01:04:09,167
Look...

1408
01:04:12,333 --> 01:04:13,958
...we're just like them.

1409
01:04:17,500 --> 01:04:19,375
They can't live without each other.

1410
01:04:20,542 --> 01:04:22,125
♪ Music continues ♪

1411
01:04:26,083 --> 01:04:27,667
[camera shutter]
[kiss]

1412
01:04:28,833 --> 01:04:30,375
[Florentina] They're seahorses.

1413
01:04:30,833 --> 01:04:32,167
♪ Music continues ♪

1414
01:04:33,250 --> 01:04:35,750
[Lucio] You're the most mysterious woman I've ever met.

1415
01:04:37,792 --> 01:04:39,458
[Martina] And the most beautiful.

1416
01:04:39,792 --> 01:04:41,167
Thank you.

1417
01:04:45,250 --> 01:04:46,583
♪ Music continues ♪

1418
01:04:47,083 --> 01:04:48,417
[Martina] Close your mouth.

1419
01:04:48,500 --> 01:04:50,000
What? She blew me away.

1420
01:04:51,125 --> 01:04:52,458
I'd do it for you.

1421
01:04:53,000 --> 01:04:55,083
If it made you happy, I'd seduce her for you.

1422
01:04:55,250 --> 01:04:57,000
I suggested the same thing with Baltha!

1423
01:04:57,125 --> 01:04:58,708
[Martina] And it never happened!

1424
01:05:00,042 --> 01:05:02,292
[Martina] Love has nothing to do with sex.

1425
01:05:02,375 --> 01:05:04,375
Oh! Did they teach you that in catechism?

1426
01:05:05,292 --> 01:05:07,000
No, you taught me that.

1427
01:05:07,917 --> 01:05:09,167
[they laugh]

1428
01:05:09,292 --> 01:05:10,750
♪ Music continues ♪

1429
01:05:16,708 --> 01:05:18,208
♪ Music ends ♪

1430
01:05:19,292 --> 01:05:21,208
[Vicente] Could I have another, please?

1431
01:05:22,458 --> 01:05:25,083
[Martina] Oh, could you do me a favor and move over a little?

1432
01:05:25,167 --> 01:05:26,625
[Loles] But why doesn't the cook help you?

1433
01:05:26,708 --> 01:05:28,667
- [Loles] Here, give me that.
- Because she's watching over dinner.

1434
01:05:28,750 --> 01:05:30,750
[Martina] Please, sit down. Your belly makes me nervous.

1435
01:05:30,833 --> 01:05:32,875
[Vicente] Hey, shouldn't we ask the cook to come out?

1436
01:05:32,958 --> 01:05:34,458
- [Vicente] So we can thank her.
- [Martina] No!

1437
01:05:34,625 --> 01:05:37,208
Sorry, it's just that she's new, and then they get spoiled...

1438
01:05:37,583 --> 01:05:40,042
- [Vicente] Thank you.
- [Loles] The chocolates are for dessert.

1439
01:05:40,125 --> 01:05:41,833
[Loles] Martina, did you know her too?

1440
01:05:41,917 --> 01:05:43,375
Florentina? Yes, of course.

1441
01:05:43,458 --> 01:05:45,333
Yes, we met her here in San Miguel.

1442
01:05:45,708 --> 01:05:47,625
At her seahorse exhibition.

1443
01:05:47,750 --> 01:05:49,125
Like my necklace!

1444
01:05:49,208 --> 01:05:51,333
That's right! I gave it to your mommy.

1445
01:05:51,500 --> 01:05:54,750
Thanks to Florentina, we learned that seahorses die of love.

1446
01:05:56,000 --> 01:05:57,375
[Lucio] When their mate dies,

1447
01:05:57,458 --> 01:05:59,958
the other dies a few days later too.

1448
01:06:00,250 --> 01:06:01,750
Oh, what is this? Hold on!

1449
01:06:01,833 --> 01:06:04,542
You brought me to your ex's house for dinner?

1450
01:06:04,625 --> 01:06:06,917
- [Lucio] No, darling...
- [Enriqueta] Faggot!

1451
01:06:07,000 --> 01:06:08,583
[Loles] I didn't expect that from you!

1452
01:06:08,667 --> 01:06:10,375
[Vicente] Loles, Loles, calm down...

1453
01:06:10,458 --> 01:06:12,875
[Lucio] Darling, that was a long time ago. It doesn't matter.

1454
01:06:12,958 --> 01:06:14,667
Besides, it was twenty-five years ago.

1455
01:06:14,750 --> 01:06:17,000
No, Martina... It was twenty-four.

1456
01:06:17,083 --> 01:06:19,500
Well, twenty-four, twenty-five... Anyway, the important thing

1457
01:06:19,792 --> 01:06:23,583
is that it's nothing, right? I'll shut up now.

1458
01:06:23,667 --> 01:06:25,708
[Loles clears throat]
[Martina] It really is nothing...

1459
01:06:26,958 --> 01:06:28,750
[Igor] Well, what happened to Florentina?

1460
01:06:28,833 --> 01:06:30,000
Did you ever see her again?

1461
01:06:30,083 --> 01:06:33,042
Yes, of course. That was the beginning of the end.

1462
01:06:33,125 --> 01:06:34,583
Right, Lucio?

1463
01:06:34,667 --> 01:06:36,125
♪ Music begins ♪

1464
01:06:37,750 --> 01:06:40,375
[Martina] And after the exhibition, Florentina

1465
01:06:40,458 --> 01:06:42,708
invited us to a party at her house.

1466
01:06:46,875 --> 01:06:48,625
♪ Music continues ♪

1467
01:06:48,708 --> 01:06:51,000
♪ When I fell in love... ♪

1468
01:06:52,542 --> 01:06:53,875
[Florentina] A toast!

1469
01:06:54,333 --> 01:06:57,792
To the day when no one asks us who we sleep with,

1470
01:06:58,250 --> 01:07:01,000
but what dreams we wake up with.

1471
01:07:01,125 --> 01:07:02,250
♪ Music continues ♪

1472
01:07:02,333 --> 01:07:04,333
I object to having to list our relationship status

1473
01:07:04,417 --> 01:07:07,833
as divorced, single, or looking for a relationship.

1474
01:07:09,208 --> 01:07:10,500
Instead, we should be free,

1475
01:07:10,792 --> 01:07:13,417
because only from that place can we create.

1476
01:07:14,292 --> 01:07:15,292
Cheers!

1477
01:07:15,375 --> 01:07:17,917
- [Martina] Cheers, then! Cheers!
- [Lucio] Cheers.

1478
01:07:18,000 --> 01:07:19,208
- [Vicente] Cheers.
- [Lucio] Cheers.

1479
01:07:19,292 --> 01:07:21,750
[Martina] So glad you're here. Cheers, cheers.

1480
01:07:22,250 --> 01:07:23,333
And that's wonderful.

1481
01:07:23,417 --> 01:07:24,500
♪ Music ends ♪

1482
01:07:24,583 --> 01:07:28,000
[Martina] There were painters, visual artists,

1483
01:07:28,500 --> 01:07:29,917
writers...

1484
01:07:30,917 --> 01:07:33,625
And we were so happy. It was like a dream.

1485
01:07:35,292 --> 01:07:36,875
Wasn't it, Lucio?

1486
01:07:37,625 --> 01:07:38,958
It was.

1487
01:07:40,833 --> 01:07:42,625
And we started dancing.

1488
01:07:42,708 --> 01:07:44,792
We had to show off our talent.

1489
01:07:44,875 --> 01:07:47,625
[Martina] ♪ Don't stand in front of me ♪

1490
01:07:47,708 --> 01:07:49,708
[Igor] Your mom is drunker than...

1491
01:07:49,792 --> 01:07:53,000
[Martina] ♪ With that hurtful look ♪

1492
01:07:53,083 --> 01:07:57,125
♪ I can understand narrow-mindedness ♪

1493
01:07:57,208 --> 01:08:01,292
♪ Put up with inexperience ♪

1494
01:08:01,875 --> 01:08:04,125
♪ But I won't tolerate ♪

1495
01:08:04,208 --> 01:08:07,708
♪ A narrow heart ♪

1496
01:08:07,792 --> 01:08:09,083
♪ Music begins ♪

1497
01:08:09,583 --> 01:08:11,042
[Vicente laughs]

1498
01:08:17,542 --> 01:08:20,167
[Loles] I think they know a dance routine.

1499
01:08:23,875 --> 01:08:25,208
♪ Music continues ♪

1500
01:08:39,000 --> 01:08:40,333
♪ Music continues ♪

1501
01:08:42,792 --> 01:08:46,000
♪ Don't ever talk like that again ♪

1502
01:08:46,375 --> 01:08:50,000
♪ Don't cheapen these relationships ♪

1503
01:08:50,083 --> 01:08:53,375
♪ If we live on love and kisses ♪

1504
01:08:53,458 --> 01:08:57,542
♪ Don't tell me about hatred and betrayal ♪

1505
01:08:57,625 --> 01:09:00,625
♪ How many things will be said? ♪

1506
01:09:01,083 --> 01:09:04,375
♪ In the war of love ♪

1507
01:09:04,708 --> 01:09:07,292
♪ Words are knives ♪

1508
01:09:07,375 --> 01:09:12,042
♪ When pride and passion wield them ♪

1509
01:09:12,708 --> 01:09:18,792
♪ You're crying and doing nothing ♪

1510
01:09:19,833 --> 01:09:22,417
♪ To understand anyone... ♪

1511
01:09:22,500 --> 01:09:23,750
♪ Music ends ♪

1512
01:09:23,875 --> 01:09:25,958
[Igor] No, no, no. That's not necessary.

1513
01:09:26,750 --> 01:09:28,042
[Loles] Come on, Lucio, sit down.

1514
01:09:28,125 --> 01:09:29,417
Pour me another mezcal.

1515
01:09:29,500 --> 01:09:31,792
- [Igor] You still have some.
- [Martina] Pour me another mezcal.

1516
01:09:31,875 --> 01:09:34,458
- [Martina] It's my house.
- [Igor] Then I'll drink that and pour you some.

1517
01:09:34,542 --> 01:09:36,375
I went a little too far...

1518
01:09:36,583 --> 01:09:38,917
Well, what happened after the dance?

1519
01:09:39,292 --> 01:09:40,667
[Enriqueta] Did you have sex?

1520
01:09:40,750 --> 01:09:42,542
[they laugh]
[Beatriz] Queta, come here!

1521
01:09:42,625 --> 01:09:45,042
[Martina] What happened was Lucio couldn't stand

1522
01:09:45,125 --> 01:09:47,500
the fact that she seduced me, and I agreed on one condition...

1523
01:09:47,583 --> 01:09:48,833
[Vicente] That you'd have a threesome!

1524
01:09:48,917 --> 01:09:50,625
[Beatriz] Queta, I said come here!

1525
01:09:50,750 --> 01:09:52,083
Not right now!

1526
01:09:52,750 --> 01:09:54,125
[Martina] No. This is how things happened, Lucio,

1527
01:09:54,208 --> 01:09:56,458
because we'd made a deal

1528
01:09:56,542 --> 01:09:58,833
that neither of us would do anything without the other's consent,

1529
01:09:58,917 --> 01:10:01,625
and that we'd be loyal, not faithful.

1530
01:10:01,708 --> 01:10:03,792
- [Igor] You've had too much to drink.
- [Vicente] That sounds good, doesn't it?

1531
01:10:03,875 --> 01:10:05,833
Vicente, please! And there's no smoking in here.

1532
01:10:05,917 --> 01:10:07,500
Why didn't you ever tell me about this?

1533
01:10:07,583 --> 01:10:09,083
- [Loles] Another pervert.
- [Igor] No, no, Loles,

1534
01:10:09,167 --> 01:10:11,083
- [Igor] it's for one of my stories.
- [Martina] No, sorry.

1535
01:10:11,167 --> 01:10:13,875
I haven't told you that Igor is a writer.

1536
01:10:13,958 --> 01:10:15,500
- [Martina] He writes plays, films...
- [Vicente] Really?

1537
01:10:15,583 --> 01:10:17,417
...novels. He's so talented!

1538
01:10:17,500 --> 01:10:18,917
- [Igor] Ghostwriter.
- [Martina] Don't start, darling.

1539
01:10:19,000 --> 01:10:20,458
Oh, you're a ghostwriter.

1540
01:10:20,542 --> 01:10:21,917
[Vicente] Does that mean you don't exist, or...?

1541
01:10:22,000 --> 01:10:23,792
Can we stop talking about that? It gives me the creeps.

1542
01:10:23,875 --> 01:10:25,958
Yes, yes. I don't exist. I do the writing. That's my talent,

1543
01:10:26,042 --> 01:10:28,458
but someone else signs it and makes money

1544
01:10:28,542 --> 01:10:30,792
and gains prestige off my back. Cheers!

1545
01:10:30,875 --> 01:10:31,917
[Martina] Cheers, yes. Enough.

1546
01:10:32,000 --> 01:10:34,125
[Loles] Of course. Now I understand his drinking problem.

1547
01:10:34,208 --> 01:10:35,958
Wait! Let's get back to our story.

1548
01:10:36,042 --> 01:10:37,125
- [Igor] Yes, yes, yes.
- [Lucio] No, no, no.

1549
01:10:37,208 --> 01:10:38,917
I'd like to know who the writer is.

1550
01:10:39,000 --> 01:10:40,500
- [Igor] Sabino Ramos.
- [Lucio] Sabino Ramos?

1551
01:10:40,583 --> 01:10:42,625
Sabino Ramos is my favorite author, man!

1552
01:10:42,708 --> 01:10:45,000
- No, no. Sabino Ramos is the one who wrote...
- [Martina] Terrible humor.

1553
01:10:45,083 --> 01:10:47,042
...Flies in the House.

1554
01:10:47,125 --> 01:10:48,667
About the neighbors who have a crisis,

1555
01:10:48,750 --> 01:10:50,875
and suddenly this other neighbor shows up,
the blond muscular one,

1556
01:10:50,958 --> 01:10:52,333
whose leg gets broken.

1557
01:10:52,417 --> 01:10:53,958
Fuck! You really know his work?

1558
01:10:54,042 --> 01:10:55,667
- [Igor] No, it's that I'm...
- [Martina] How your friends have changed,

1559
01:10:55,750 --> 01:10:57,000
Lucio.

1560
01:10:57,083 --> 01:10:58,250
Hey, man, you have to do something!

1561
01:10:58,333 --> 01:11:00,333
[Igor] Well, I've got one last novel left

1562
01:11:00,417 --> 01:11:01,792
that I can't finish writing.

1563
01:11:01,875 --> 01:11:03,042
[Loles] But why? Do you have writer's block?

1564
01:11:03,125 --> 01:11:04,917
No, no. It's a very personal story.

1565
01:11:05,083 --> 01:11:06,458
[Igor] The Captain's Son.

1566
01:11:06,542 --> 01:11:09,250
I'm afraid to finish it and have them take it away from me again.

1567
01:11:09,333 --> 01:11:11,625
- [Lucio] Don't give it to him.
- [Vicente] I mean, what have you got to lose?

1568
01:11:11,708 --> 01:11:13,458
Absolutely nothing.
[laughs]

1569
01:11:13,542 --> 01:11:15,625
No! They'd throw me in jail. That's what could...

1570
01:11:15,708 --> 01:11:17,208
[Lucio] Nobody's going to throw you in jail.

1571
01:11:17,292 --> 01:11:20,000
I mean, if this came to light, he'd lose what
matters most to him.

1572
01:11:20,083 --> 01:11:21,333
His reputation, right?

1573
01:11:21,417 --> 01:11:24,042
You've given him so much. That contract is over now.

1574
01:11:24,125 --> 01:11:25,500
Oh! I love you, darling...

1575
01:11:25,583 --> 01:11:27,625
[Martina] Okay, enough...
[cheers and claps]

1576
01:11:28,125 --> 01:11:30,667
...we've solved Igor's life. You're a free man.

1577
01:11:30,750 --> 01:11:32,917
Now let's sort out our own story...

1578
01:11:33,000 --> 01:11:34,208
You were at the part where they had a threesome.

1579
01:11:34,292 --> 01:11:35,292
[Martina] Oh, right.

1580
01:11:35,375 --> 01:11:38,125
To satisfy the little darling's desires.

1581
01:11:38,208 --> 01:11:39,583
[Beatriz] Queta, come over here!

1582
01:11:39,667 --> 01:11:41,833
Nobody's going anywhere. Sit down!

1583
01:11:41,917 --> 01:11:43,708
Because this is my house and this is my daughter!

1584
01:11:43,792 --> 01:11:44,958
[Igor] You're shouting too much.

1585
01:11:45,042 --> 01:11:46,500
[Lucio] Martina, this is between you and me.

1586
01:11:46,583 --> 01:11:47,875
[Martina] That's what I thought,

1587
01:11:47,958 --> 01:11:49,333
but you went and told everyone.

1588
01:11:49,417 --> 01:11:51,250
[Lucio] That's not how it happened. It wasn't.

1589
01:11:51,333 --> 01:11:52,583
- [Martina] "That's not how it happened."
- [Vicente] What happened, then?

1590
01:11:52,667 --> 01:11:54,750
You know what? I feel liberated!

1591
01:11:54,833 --> 01:11:55,833
[laughter]

1592
01:11:55,917 --> 01:11:57,167
[Martina] Because I've spent twenty-five years

1593
01:11:57,250 --> 01:11:58,833
waiting to confront you about this.

1594
01:11:58,917 --> 01:12:01,167
[Lucio] Twenty-four fucking years! Why do you keep saying that?

1595
01:12:01,250 --> 01:12:02,292
[Vicente laughs]

1596
01:12:02,375 --> 01:12:03,792
[Igor] Yeah, this is all very funny...

1597
01:12:03,917 --> 01:12:05,917
- [Loles] Vicente, please!
- [Lucio] It was twenty-four, man.

1598
01:12:06,000 --> 01:12:07,375
[Loles] Please, Vicente!

1599
01:12:07,458 --> 01:12:09,583
It's just that this is so crazy...

1600
01:12:09,667 --> 01:12:12,833
- [Loles] And what happened?
- [Martina] Well, we kept exploring

1601
01:12:12,917 --> 01:12:15,000
what Florentina and her friends were suggesting to us,

1602
01:12:15,083 --> 01:12:16,417
[Martina] the ideas they'd put in our heads.

1603
01:12:16,500 --> 01:12:18,500
- [Martina] Right?
- [Lucio] Yes.

1604
01:12:18,583 --> 01:12:20,167
- [Igor] Exploring...
- [Loles] Vicente, stop...!

1605
01:12:20,250 --> 01:12:21,750
[Vicente laughs]

1606
01:12:23,333 --> 01:12:25,292
Well, there was just one loose end.

1607
01:12:25,375 --> 01:12:27,792
Of course, Balthazar, our ballet teacher.

1608
01:12:27,875 --> 01:12:30,417
- [Martina] Write that down.
- [Loles] The one with the chocolates...

1609
01:12:31,500 --> 01:12:33,167
♪ Music begins ♪

1610
01:12:41,792 --> 01:12:44,500
♪ She saw him leave that place ♪

1611
01:12:45,250 --> 01:12:46,792
♪ Now she knew the truth... ♪

1612
01:12:46,875 --> 01:12:48,792
You're the one who's going to lose here.

1613
01:12:49,083 --> 01:12:52,083
♪ And she made up her mind ♪

1614
01:12:54,708 --> 01:12:56,583
♪ Music continues ♪

1615
01:12:59,250 --> 01:13:01,125
[Lucio] Amelia put things in my head...

1616
01:13:01,208 --> 01:13:02,542
- [Loles] The unscrupulous girl...
- [Vicente] Who?

1617
01:13:02,625 --> 01:13:03,625
Shut up.

1618
01:13:03,708 --> 01:13:05,750
And everything got out of control.

1619
01:13:05,833 --> 01:13:08,625
♪ After writing down the address ♪

1620
01:13:09,958 --> 01:13:12,125
♪ Fighting back tears ♪

1621
01:13:12,500 --> 01:13:15,708
♪ How could you do this to me? ♪

1622
01:13:15,875 --> 01:13:18,833
♪ When I would have loved you to the end ♪

1623
01:13:19,708 --> 01:13:22,375
♪ I know you'll regret it ♪

1624
01:13:22,458 --> 01:13:25,208
♪ The deserted street, a perfect night... ♪

1625
01:13:25,292 --> 01:13:27,917
[Amelia] Martina, we'll go on ahead to your house, okay?

1626
01:13:29,417 --> 01:13:35,167
♪ One well-aimed blow and it was all over between them ♪

1627
01:13:35,250 --> 01:13:38,125
[silence] No, Lucio. You broke a promise.

1628
01:13:40,625 --> 01:13:41,875
♪ Music continues ♪

1629
01:13:41,958 --> 01:13:45,083
♪ She didn't even want to look ♪

1630
01:13:45,167 --> 01:13:48,250
♪ She'd never go back ♪

1631
01:13:48,792 --> 01:13:51,458
♪ Once and never again, Saint Thomas ♪

1632
01:13:52,042 --> 01:13:55,083
♪ How could you do this to me? ♪

1633
01:13:55,458 --> 01:13:58,500
♪ When I would have loved you to the end ♪

1634
01:13:59,250 --> 01:14:01,917
♪ I know you'll regret it! ♪

1635
01:14:02,000 --> 01:14:05,083
♪ The deserted street, a perfect night ♪

1636
01:14:05,292 --> 01:14:07,167
♪ A car with no lights... ♪

1637
01:14:07,250 --> 01:14:10,250
We were alone, Lucio. Nobody else knew what happened.

1638
01:14:10,333 --> 01:14:12,333
Amelia left the video recording.

1639
01:14:13,208 --> 01:14:14,875
- [Martina] What video?
- [Lucio] "What video?"

1640
01:14:14,958 --> 01:14:16,583
- [Vicente] What video?
- [Loles] What? What happened?

1641
01:14:16,667 --> 01:14:19,625
Nothing. We were just satisfying the girl's desires.

1642
01:14:19,708 --> 01:14:21,292
No, no, no. Tell them what happened.

1643
01:14:21,375 --> 01:14:23,542
Balthazar was accused of sexual abuse.

1644
01:14:23,625 --> 01:14:24,875
Oh my God!

1645
01:14:25,417 --> 01:14:27,458
- [Martina] And you testified against him.
- [Lucio] That's not what happened, damn it!

1646
01:14:27,542 --> 01:14:29,875
You handed over the photos, Lucio, for God's sake!

1647
01:14:30,042 --> 01:14:31,375
[Martina] Because on the night with Balthazar,

1648
01:14:31,458 --> 01:14:34,250
Lucio saw fit to come to my house and seduce my sister,

1649
01:14:34,333 --> 01:14:36,417
who was madly in love with him.

1650
01:14:36,875 --> 01:14:38,875
[Enriqueta] Mom!
[Martina shushes]

1651
01:14:39,083 --> 01:14:41,083
- [Lucio] I was jealous! What do you expect?
- [Martina] So what?

1652
01:14:41,167 --> 01:14:42,792
You slept with her sister?

1653
01:14:43,500 --> 01:14:44,542
You bastard!

1654
01:14:44,625 --> 01:14:46,458
[Beatriz shouts] Queta, come to the kitchen, please!

1655
01:14:46,542 --> 01:14:47,667
Don't move! Don't move.

1656
01:14:47,750 --> 01:14:49,000
It's the chef! Let's hear it for the chef!
[applause]

1657
01:14:49,083 --> 01:14:50,417
[Martina] You're the one going to the kitchen!

1658
01:14:50,500 --> 01:14:53,458
What are you doing here? Go back!

1659
01:14:53,542 --> 01:14:54,583
What do you think you're doing? You...!

1660
01:14:54,667 --> 01:14:56,125
[Lucio] Martina, yes, I went to get the photographs,

1661
01:14:56,208 --> 01:14:57,875
but the only one there was you, Beatriz!

1662
01:14:57,958 --> 01:14:59,250
The cook is her sister!

1663
01:14:59,333 --> 01:15:01,000
- [Martina] Enough, enough.
- [Lucio] I never seduced you!

1664
01:15:01,083 --> 01:15:03,125
Besides, you saw me put the photos in my backpack!

1665
01:15:03,417 --> 01:15:04,625
♪ Music begins ♪

1666
01:15:04,708 --> 01:15:06,042
Romeo!

1667
01:15:10,000 --> 01:15:11,833
[Igor] Photographs? What photos?

1668
01:15:12,125 --> 01:15:13,625
[Martina] The ones Florentina took of us.

1669
01:15:13,708 --> 01:15:15,542
[Lucio] Someone else knew where those photographs were,

1670
01:15:15,625 --> 01:15:16,833
didn't they, Beatriz?

1671
01:15:16,917 --> 01:15:18,167
They're in his backpack.

1672
01:15:18,292 --> 01:15:19,958
♪ Music continues ♪

1673
01:15:21,542 --> 01:15:22,542
[Martina] Never mind,

1674
01:15:22,625 --> 01:15:25,083
who cares about all this after twenty-five years, for God's sake!

1675
01:15:25,167 --> 01:15:26,333
I do.

1676
01:15:26,708 --> 01:15:28,167
Check his backpack.

1677
01:15:29,250 --> 01:15:30,583
♪ Music continues ♪

1678
01:15:31,458 --> 01:15:33,167
[hall monitor] That's all the evidence.

1679
01:15:39,458 --> 01:15:40,792
♪ Music continues ♪

1680
01:15:40,875 --> 01:15:42,750
- [Lucio] Immoral!
- [Martina] Immoral.

1681
01:15:42,833 --> 01:15:44,042
Immoral!

1682
01:15:44,375 --> 01:15:46,042
[shouting] Immoral!

1683
01:15:46,208 --> 01:15:47,542
♪ Music continues ♪

1684
01:15:52,250 --> 01:15:53,333
[shouting] Immoral!

1685
01:15:53,417 --> 01:15:55,250
[Mom] Hey! Take this.

1686
01:15:56,208 --> 01:15:58,917
Get your things out quickly, Martina, for God's sake!

1687
01:15:59,000 --> 01:16:00,333
♪ Music fades ♪

1688
01:16:01,167 --> 01:16:02,708
I was accused too.

1689
01:16:02,792 --> 01:16:04,375
[Loles] Write it down, write it down!

1690
01:16:04,458 --> 01:16:06,542
What was the teacher's name?

1691
01:16:06,625 --> 01:16:07,667
Balthazar.

1692
01:16:08,000 --> 01:16:09,333
♪ Music swells ♪

1693
01:16:11,333 --> 01:16:12,583
[shouting] Guilty!

1694
01:16:13,458 --> 01:16:16,083
[Igor] After all this, you never saw each other again?

1695
01:16:16,333 --> 01:16:17,458
No, we did.

1696
01:16:17,583 --> 01:16:18,667
♪ Music continues ♪

1697
01:16:18,750 --> 01:16:21,833
We saw each other a week later to make love one last time.

1698
01:16:22,500 --> 01:16:23,917
We recorded ourselves again...

1699
01:16:32,667 --> 01:16:34,000
♪ Music continues ♪

1700
01:16:38,792 --> 01:16:41,375
We wanted to say goodbye to the last corner of the world.

1701
01:16:43,042 --> 01:16:46,250
Martina, I wanted you to know the truth, but
you wouldn't let me explain.

1702
01:16:47,292 --> 01:16:48,958
I told you: never again, Lucio.

1703
01:16:49,042 --> 01:16:50,417
[Martina] Never again.

1704
01:16:51,333 --> 01:16:52,667
♪ Music continues ♪

1705
01:16:55,917 --> 01:16:57,667
And I was stupid enough to listen to you!

1706
01:17:02,708 --> 01:17:04,125
Sorry, sorry.

1707
01:17:05,125 --> 01:17:06,417
♪ Music ends ♪

1708
01:17:09,292 --> 01:17:11,167
- [Loles] Vicente...
- [Vicente] Huh? What's wrong?

1709
01:17:11,833 --> 01:17:13,292
I think my water broke.

1710
01:17:13,375 --> 01:17:15,083
- [Lucio] What? I'm going to be a dad!
- [Vicente] I'm going to be a dad...

1711
01:17:15,167 --> 01:17:16,750
You're going to be a dad. You're going to be a dad, you bastard!

1712
01:17:16,833 --> 01:17:19,083
[Loles] A doctor! Call your doctor, for God's sake.

1713
01:17:19,292 --> 01:17:21,375
Roberta, tell your mother to call the doctor!

1714
01:17:21,542 --> 01:17:22,917
My name is Enriqueta!

1715
01:17:23,000 --> 01:17:25,208
I'm trying to explain. Let me explain.

1716
01:17:25,292 --> 01:17:27,000
- [Enriqueta] Mom!
- [Beatriz and Martina] What?

1717
01:17:27,083 --> 01:17:29,458
- [Enriqueta] Call a doctor.
- [Beatriz] No, just drink some water,

1718
01:17:29,542 --> 01:17:31,917
- [Beatriz] and you'll feel better.
- [Enriqueta] It's for the pregnant lady.

1719
01:17:32,000 --> 01:17:33,750
Oh, is she feeling sick? Let's see. Here's a number.

1720
01:17:33,833 --> 01:17:35,167
Amelia hated Balthazar.

1721
01:17:35,250 --> 01:17:37,042
[Martina] No, Amelia hated everything close to me.

1722
01:17:37,125 --> 01:17:40,083
Exactly! But I knew the photos existed.

1723
01:17:40,292 --> 01:17:41,708
But she had a video!

1724
01:17:41,792 --> 01:17:44,000
- [Enriqueta] What's the address?
- [Martina] Terraplén, ten.

1725
01:17:44,083 --> 01:17:46,417
Hey! She accused me and said God would punish me.

1726
01:17:46,500 --> 01:17:48,208
So I told her where the photos were.

1727
01:17:48,625 --> 01:17:52,208
And Amelia put them, along with the video, into Lucio's backpack.

1728
01:17:52,625 --> 01:17:55,083
- So you'd never find out.
- [Martina] Don't worry.

1729
01:17:55,167 --> 01:17:56,583
God won't punish you...

1730
01:17:57,375 --> 01:17:58,958
...Jehovah will, you bitch.

1731
01:17:59,042 --> 01:18:00,958
Forgive me, please!

1732
01:18:01,042 --> 01:18:02,250
♪ Music begins ♪

1733
01:18:02,333 --> 01:18:03,500
[Lucio] I'm going to be a dad!

1734
01:18:03,583 --> 01:18:04,875
I'm going to be a dad!

1735
01:18:04,958 --> 01:18:07,208
[Martina] You've really had trouble coming to
terms with it, haven't you?

1736
01:18:07,292 --> 01:18:08,667
[Loles] The baby's coming!

1737
01:18:08,750 --> 01:18:10,042
No! You've still got time.

1738
01:18:10,125 --> 01:18:11,125
Well, I don't know.

1739
01:18:11,208 --> 01:18:12,458
Oh God... Oh!

1740
01:18:12,667 --> 01:18:14,542
- [Martina] Beatriz!
- [Vicente] Are you okay, darling?

1741
01:18:14,625 --> 01:18:15,875
No, let's go. Come on, let's go.

1742
01:18:15,958 --> 01:18:17,625
[Igor] No, no, no. Sit down!

1743
01:18:17,708 --> 01:18:19,292
Yes, yes. It's dangerous. It's dangerous.

1744
01:18:19,375 --> 01:18:21,625
- [Loles] Why?
- [Igor] Because she could fall. I know about these things.

1745
01:18:22,000 --> 01:18:24,083
[Igor] Let's get back to the story, please!

1746
01:18:24,667 --> 01:18:26,250
What a fantastic novel you've got here, darling.

1747
01:18:26,333 --> 01:18:28,417
If this doesn't make you rich, you're hopeless.

1748
01:18:28,500 --> 01:18:30,333
And Amelia accused you?

1749
01:18:30,417 --> 01:18:32,042
Yes, that unscrupulous girl!

1750
01:18:32,125 --> 01:18:34,208
She was always manipulating everything to suit herself.

1751
01:18:34,292 --> 01:18:36,083
Oh! That bitch is going to be president someday.

1752
01:18:36,167 --> 01:18:38,458
She was in love with you, maybe more than we
were with each other.

1753
01:18:38,542 --> 01:18:39,625
Oh, what's wrong with you, Lucio?
[doorbell]

1754
01:18:39,708 --> 01:18:40,708
[Vicente] The doctor is here!

1755
01:18:40,792 --> 01:18:42,125
Open the gate for him, Beatriz.

1756
01:18:42,208 --> 01:18:43,833
[Igor] But I missed the middle of the story.
Did you forgive her or not?

1757
01:18:43,917 --> 01:18:45,833
Poor thing is all alone. Come on, my queen.

1758
01:18:45,917 --> 01:18:48,250
Everything will be fine. Come on, stay strong.

1759
01:18:48,333 --> 01:18:50,333
[Martina] Why don't you unfasten her seat belt, you idiot?

1760
01:18:50,417 --> 01:18:51,750
- [Vicente] What?
- [Martina] This is too tight.

1761
01:18:51,833 --> 01:18:53,375
- [Loles] Vicente, my cardigan.
- [Vicente] The cardigan, the cardigan...

1762
01:18:53,458 --> 01:18:54,750
[Martina] Who's got the cardigan? The doula?

1763
01:18:54,833 --> 01:18:57,208
- Who has the phone number for...?
- [Loles] Vicente, did you grab my purse?

1764
01:18:57,292 --> 01:18:59,375
- [Martina] Here, take this, please!
- [Loles] I can't walk in heels.

1765
01:18:59,458 --> 01:19:00,708
[Vicente] Your cardigan, darling.

1766
01:19:00,792 --> 01:19:01,917
Shall we go? Who's the father?

1767
01:19:02,000 --> 01:19:03,333
- [Lucio] Me.
- [Vicente] Me!

1768
01:19:05,083 --> 01:19:07,125
Vicente, they're talking to you.

1769
01:19:08,542 --> 01:19:10,208
You're the father. Will you come with me, please?

1770
01:19:10,292 --> 01:19:11,958
What a shame! We were doing so well.

1771
01:19:12,042 --> 01:19:14,292
- [Martina] You too?
- [Loles] I'm a natural actress, you know.

1772
01:19:14,375 --> 01:19:17,042
But nature takes over. I'm sorry!

1773
01:19:17,208 --> 01:19:18,542
[Loles] Let's go, let's go.

1774
01:19:18,625 --> 01:19:20,333
- So you're still lying, Lucio.
- [Lucio] No, no, no.

1775
01:19:20,417 --> 01:19:21,583
For God's sake, he's my son too!

1776
01:19:21,667 --> 01:19:22,667
Only biologically.

1777
01:19:22,750 --> 01:19:23,750
But how? Are you crazy?

1778
01:19:23,833 --> 01:19:25,542
[Loles] Well, if it's a boy, we'll name him Lucio.

1779
01:19:25,625 --> 01:19:27,083
[Martina] No, you two are...

1780
01:19:27,167 --> 01:19:28,667
[Martina calls out] Let us know! Let us know.

1781
01:19:28,750 --> 01:19:29,875
[Lucio] I love you, man!

1782
01:19:31,625 --> 01:19:34,292
But you didn't even want children, Lucio.

1783
01:19:34,375 --> 01:19:35,500
You know me well.

1784
01:19:37,042 --> 01:19:38,042
I mean,

1785
01:19:38,125 --> 01:19:40,542
- [Martina] she's not even your wife.
- [Lucio] No.

1786
01:19:40,750 --> 01:19:41,958
But the baby does have my genes.

1787
01:19:42,042 --> 01:19:43,375
- [Lucio] That's another story!
- [Martina] No, what's wrong with you?

1788
01:19:43,458 --> 01:19:45,917
- [Martina] Lucio, you're sick.
- [Lucio] I know, I know! It's absurd!

1789
01:19:46,000 --> 01:19:48,917
It's completely absurd, but I want you to know I waited for you.

1790
01:19:49,000 --> 01:19:50,625
- [Martina] Why didn't you look for me?
- [Lucio] I did!

1791
01:19:50,708 --> 01:19:52,208
I went, but they'd sent you away. I sent you letters.

1792
01:19:52,292 --> 01:19:54,583
- [Martina] What letters?
- [Beatriz] I kept them in my nightstand!

1793
01:19:56,167 --> 01:19:57,667
[Beatriz screams]
[Igor] Martina!

1794
01:19:57,750 --> 01:19:59,667
- [Igor] Wait, Martina!
- [Enriqueta] Auntie, calm down!

1795
01:19:59,750 --> 01:20:01,333
- [Beatriz] Sorry!
- [Martina] Come here, you bitch, I'll...!

1796
01:20:01,417 --> 01:20:02,708
- [Martina] Let go of me!
- [Beatriz] No!

1797
01:20:02,792 --> 01:20:04,917
- [Beatriz] I begged God! I prayed!
- [Martina] Shut up!

1798
01:20:05,000 --> 01:20:07,250
- [Vicente] What's happening, doctor?
- You know what? We won't make it.

1799
01:20:07,333 --> 01:20:08,708
- [Vicente] What?
- [doctor] We're going to stop.

1800
01:20:08,792 --> 01:20:10,833
[doctor] We're pulling over. It's better if we stop.

1801
01:20:10,917 --> 01:20:12,500
Tell them to pull over.

1802
01:20:12,583 --> 01:20:13,917
[ambulance siren]
[Vicente] Stop!

1803
01:20:14,250 --> 01:20:15,375
Stop!

1804
01:20:15,958 --> 01:20:17,458
[Vicente] Tell them to stop, damn it!

1805
01:20:17,542 --> 01:20:19,583
[Vicente shouts] Brake! Brake!

1806
01:20:19,667 --> 01:20:21,125
[ambulance siren]
[tires screeching]

1807
01:20:21,208 --> 01:20:22,917
[Beatriz] Get off! He's groping me!

1808
01:20:23,125 --> 01:20:24,792
[Beatriz] You... bitch!

1809
01:20:25,208 --> 01:20:26,958
[Beatriz] Come here, I'll pour you some.

1810
01:20:27,417 --> 01:20:29,333
[Martina complains]

1811
01:20:29,417 --> 01:20:32,917
[Beatriz] Why, Martina? Please forgive me!

1812
01:20:33,542 --> 01:20:34,875
[they laugh]

1813
01:20:35,667 --> 01:20:36,917
Lucio.

1814
01:20:37,458 --> 01:20:38,875
I went looking for you too.

1815
01:20:38,958 --> 01:20:40,583
[Martina] I missed you so much.

1816
01:20:41,250 --> 01:20:42,708
[heavy breathing]

1817
01:20:48,083 --> 01:20:49,375
[Lucio laughs]

1818
01:20:56,417 --> 01:20:58,417
I looked for you among the dancers,

1819
01:20:58,500 --> 01:21:00,458
hoping I'd find you.

1820
01:21:00,708 --> 01:21:03,083
No. I never danced again.

1821
01:21:03,333 --> 01:21:06,167
And I became the ballet teacher of San Miguel.

1822
01:21:08,042 --> 01:21:10,875
I moved here to see if I could remember

1823
01:21:10,958 --> 01:21:13,042
that we could have been seahorses.

1824
01:21:15,542 --> 01:21:18,167
He's not my husband either.

1825
01:21:18,458 --> 01:21:20,125
Martina, the rent.

1826
01:21:20,208 --> 01:21:21,500
[Martina shushes]

1827
01:21:21,708 --> 01:21:23,750
And she's not my daughter.

1828
01:21:24,083 --> 01:21:25,708
My aunt is an old maid.

1829
01:21:28,625 --> 01:21:31,083
Can you leave us alone, please?

1830
01:21:31,208 --> 01:21:33,208
♪ Music begins ♪

1831
01:21:36,125 --> 01:21:38,750
That day, after leaving the building,

1832
01:21:40,333 --> 01:21:42,000
I went downstairs to look for the little seahorse.

1833
01:21:43,292 --> 01:21:46,125
I did the same, but I knew you'd found it.

1834
01:21:51,875 --> 01:21:53,875
♪ Music continues ♪

1835
01:21:56,250 --> 01:21:57,333
Martina...

1836
01:22:07,125 --> 01:22:08,125
Look, Lucio.

1837
01:22:10,417 --> 01:22:13,208
[Martina] Florentina gave me this when I moved here.

1838
01:22:14,375 --> 01:22:15,708
[they laugh]

1839
01:22:17,167 --> 01:22:18,583
♪ Music continues ♪

1840
01:22:20,417 --> 01:22:21,750
[Martina] Good night.

1841
01:22:24,500 --> 01:22:26,792
It was important to me that you knew the truth.

1842
01:22:28,333 --> 01:22:29,625
[Martina] It's late.

1843
01:22:30,292 --> 01:22:31,875
[Lucio] It's never too late, Martina.

1844
01:22:32,208 --> 01:22:34,250
No. I mean it's getting late. We should get some rest, right?

1845
01:22:34,333 --> 01:22:35,333
♪ Music ends ♪

1846
01:22:35,417 --> 01:22:37,083
A lot of emotions for one night, huh?

1847
01:22:37,167 --> 01:22:38,167
[Martina] Yes.

1848
01:22:38,250 --> 01:22:39,333
Good night.

1849
01:22:51,667 --> 01:22:52,667
Goodbye.

1850
01:23:00,542 --> 01:23:02,125
[crickets chirping]

1851
01:23:18,792 --> 01:23:20,208
[knocking at door]

1852
01:23:26,750 --> 01:23:28,333
[knocking at door]

1853
01:23:33,375 --> 01:23:34,583
[Martina] What happened?

1854
01:23:34,667 --> 01:23:36,083
♪ Music begins ♪

1855
01:23:38,125 --> 01:23:39,458
I forgot my jacket.

1856
01:23:39,542 --> 01:23:40,958
[heavy breathing]

1857
01:23:54,833 --> 01:23:56,542
♪ Music continues ♪

1858
01:24:19,333 --> 01:24:20,667
♪ Music continues ♪

1859
01:24:21,417 --> 01:24:25,042
♪ Somewhere in a big country ♪

1860
01:24:27,792 --> 01:24:30,875
♪ They forgot to build ♪

1861
01:24:34,208 --> 01:24:38,083
♪ A home where the sun doesn't burn ♪

1862
01:24:40,417 --> 01:24:41,542
♪ And at birth... ♪
♪ Music ends ♪

1863
01:24:41,625 --> 01:24:43,458
[Amelia] Today I've decided to address

1864
01:24:43,542 --> 01:24:45,667
all of you,

1865
01:24:45,750 --> 01:24:49,042
to explain why I tore down that old building...

1866
01:24:50,250 --> 01:24:52,042
...because I have nothing to hide.

1867
01:24:53,167 --> 01:24:56,083
[Amelia] I've worked for twenty-five years

1868
01:24:56,375 --> 01:24:59,042
in my photography business,

1869
01:24:59,458 --> 01:25:00,583
developing film...

1870
01:25:01,208 --> 01:25:02,458
♪ Music begins ♪

1871
01:25:17,708 --> 01:25:19,792
♪ I'll begin ♪

1872
01:25:21,625 --> 01:25:23,333
♪ By saying that ♪

1873
01:25:24,292 --> 01:25:27,250
♪ Neither of us ♪

1874
01:25:27,500 --> 01:25:29,667
♪ Is to blame ♪

1875
01:25:33,375 --> 01:25:35,417
♪ And in the end ♪

1876
01:25:37,250 --> 01:25:39,292
♪ It'll work out ♪

1877
01:25:40,292 --> 01:25:43,000
♪ Let's stop drifting ♪

1878
01:25:43,083 --> 01:25:45,708
♪ In a sea of doubts ♪

1879
01:25:48,375 --> 01:25:52,250
♪ Two runaway horses ♪

1880
01:25:52,333 --> 01:25:55,875
♪ With the world under our arms ♪

1881
01:25:56,042 --> 01:26:00,792
♪ Escaping together to nowhere ♪

1882
01:26:05,875 --> 01:26:09,458
♪ We find each other again ♪

1883
01:26:09,667 --> 01:26:13,625
♪ After so many years ♪

1884
01:26:13,708 --> 01:26:17,458
♪ Just one more time ♪

1885
01:26:21,583 --> 01:26:24,875
♪ Holding hands ♪

1886
01:26:25,375 --> 01:26:29,125
♪ With the world under our arms ♪

1887
01:26:29,625 --> 01:26:33,667
♪ Without looking back ♪

1888
01:26:40,375 --> 01:26:42,208
♪ And what does it matter? ♪

1889
01:26:43,125 --> 01:26:45,958
♪ If we were to fail ♪

1890
01:26:46,958 --> 01:26:49,958
♪ We won't change ♪

1891
01:26:50,042 --> 01:26:52,500
♪ This madness ♪

1892
01:26:55,167 --> 01:26:59,208
♪ Two runaway horses ♪

1893
